#: src/introduction.md:1
msgid "\\[!Tip\\] Impatient readers may head straight to [Quick Start](quick-start.md)."
msgstr "\\[!Tip\\] 心急的读者可以直接跳到 [快速开始](quick-start.md)。"

#: src/introduction.md:4
msgid "\\[!Important\\] Using a previous version of Kubebuilder? Check the legacy documentation for [v1](https://book-v1.book.kubebuilder.io), [v2](https://book-v2.book.kubebuilder.io) or [v3](https://book-v3.book.kubebuilder.io)."
msgstr "\\[!Important\\] 仍在使用旧版 Kubebuilder？请查看遗留文档：[v1](https://book-v1.book.kubebuilder.io)、[v2](https://book-v2.book.kubebuilder.io) 或 [v3](https://book-v3.book.kubebuilder.io)。"

#: src/introduction.md:7
msgid "Who is this for"
msgstr "这适合谁"

#: src/introduction.md:9
msgid "Users of Kubernetes"
msgstr "Kubernetes 的用户"

#: src/introduction.md:11
msgid "Users of Kubernetes will develop a deeper understanding of Kubernetes through learning the fundamental concepts behind how APIs are designed and implemented.  This book will teach readers how to develop their own Kubernetes APIs and the principles from which the core Kubernetes APIs are designed."
msgstr "Kubernetes 用户将通过学习 API 设计和实现的基本概念，深入理解 Kubernetes。 本书将教会读者如何开发自己的 Kubernetes API 以及核心 Kubernetes API 设计的原则。"

#: src/introduction.md:16 src/introduction.md:32
msgid "Including:"
msgstr "包括："

#: src/introduction.md:18
msgid "The structure of Kubernetes APIs and Resources"
msgstr "Kubernetes API 和资源的结构"

#: src/introduction.md:19
msgid "API versioning semantics"
msgstr "API 版本控制语义"

#: src/introduction.md:20
msgid "Self-healing"
msgstr "自我修复"

#: src/introduction.md:21
msgid "Garbage Collection and Finalizers"
msgstr "垃圾收集与终结器"

#: src/introduction.md:22
msgid "Declarative vs Imperative APIs"
msgstr "声明式 API 与 命令式 API"

#: src/introduction.md:23
msgid "Level-Based vs Edge-Based APIs"
msgstr "基于级别 vs 基于边沿的 API"

#: src/introduction.md:24
msgid "Resources vs Subresources"
msgstr "资源与子资源"

#: src/introduction.md:26
msgid "Kubernetes API extension developers"
msgstr "Kubernetes API 扩展开发者"

#: src/introduction.md:28
msgid "API extension developers will learn the principles and concepts behind implementing canonical Kubernetes APIs, as well as simple tools and libraries for rapid execution.  This book covers pitfalls and misconceptions that extension developers commonly encounter."
msgstr "API 扩展开发者将学习实现规范 Kubernetes API 的原则和概念，以及用于快速执行的简单工具和库。 本书涵盖了扩展开发者常遇到的陷阱和误解。"

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid "How to batch multiple events into a single reconciliation call"
msgstr "如何将多个事件批量合并到一次对账调用中"

#: src/introduction.md:35
msgid "How to configure periodic reconciliation"
msgstr "如何配置定期对账"

#: src/introduction.md:36
msgid "_Forthcoming_"
msgstr "_即将到来_"

#: src/introduction.md:37
msgid "When to use the lister cache vs live lookups"
msgstr "何时使用列出缓存与实时查找"

#: src/introduction.md:38
msgid "Garbage Collection vs Finalizers"
msgstr "垃圾回收（Garbage Collection）与终结器（Finalizers）"

#: src/introduction.md:39
msgid "How to use Declarative vs Webhook Validation"
msgstr "如何使用声明式验证与 Webhook 验证"

#: src/introduction.md:40
msgid "How to implement API versioning"
msgstr "如何实现 API 版本控制"

#: src/introduction.md:42
msgid "Why Kubernetes APIs"
msgstr "为什么选择 Kubernetes API"

#: src/introduction.md:44
msgid "Kubernetes APIs provide consistent and well-defined endpoints for objects adhering to a consistent and rich structure."
msgstr "Kubernetes API 为遵循一致且丰富结构的对象提供统一且定义清晰的端点。"

#: src/introduction.md:47
msgid "This approach has fostered a rich ecosystem of tools and libraries for working with Kubernetes APIs."
msgstr "这种方式促进了丰富的工具和库生态系统与 Kubernetes API 进行交互。"

#: src/introduction.md:50
msgid "Users work with the APIs through declaring objects as _YAML_ or _JSON_ config, and using common tooling to manage the objects."
msgstr "用户通过将对象声明为 _YAML_ 或 _JSON_ 配置，并使用通用工具来管理这些对象，从而使用 API。"

#: src/introduction.md:53
msgid "Building services as Kubernetes APIs provides many advantages to plain old REST, including:"
msgstr "将服务构建为 Kubernetes API 相较于传统的REST，有以下优势："

#: src/introduction.md:55
msgid "Hosted API endpoints, storage, and validation."
msgstr "托管的 API 网络端点、存储和验证。"

#: src/introduction.md:56
msgid "Rich tooling and CLIs such as `kubectl` and `kustomize`."
msgstr "丰富的工具和命令行接口，例如 `kubectl` 和 `kustomize`。"

#: src/introduction.md:57
msgid "Support for AuthN and granular AuthZ."
msgstr "支持身份验证（AuthN）和细粒度授权（AuthZ）。"

#: src/introduction.md:58
msgid "Support for API evolution through API versioning and conversion."
msgstr "通过 API 版本控制和转换并且支持 API 版本演进。"

#: src/introduction.md:59
msgid "Facilitation of adaptive / self-healing APIs that continuously respond to changes in the system state without user intervention."
msgstr "促进自适应/自愈 API 的实现，它们能够在没有用户干预的情况下持续响应系统状态的变化。"

#: src/introduction.md:61
msgid "Kubernetes as a hosting environment"
msgstr "Kubernetes 是一个托管环境"

#: src/introduction.md:63
msgid "Developers may build and publish their own Kubernetes APIs for installation into running Kubernetes clusters."
msgstr "开发者可以构建并发布自己的 Kubernetes API，方便安装到运行中的 Kubernetes 集群中。"

#: src/introduction.md:66
msgid "Contribution"
msgstr "贡献"

#: src/introduction.md:68
msgid "If you like to contribute to either this book or the code, please be kind enough to read our [Contribution](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md) guidelines first."
msgstr "如果您想为本书或代码贡献内容，请先阅读我们的 [贡献](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md) 指南。"

#: src/introduction.md:71
msgid "Resources"
msgstr "资源"

#: src/introduction.md:73
msgid "Repository: [sigs.k8s.io/kubebuilder](https://sigs.k8s.io/kubebuilder)"
msgstr "仓库: [sigs.k8s.io/kubebuilder](https://sigs.k8s.io/kubebuilder)"

#: src/introduction.md:75
msgid "Slack channel: [\\#kubebuilder](http://slack.k8s.io/#kubebuilder)"
msgstr "Slack频道：[\\#kubebuilder](http://slack.k8s.io/#kubebuilder)"

#: src/introduction.md:77
msgid "Google Group: [kubebuilder@googlegroups.com](https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/kubebuilder)"
msgstr "Google 群组: [kubebuilder@googlegroups.com](https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/kubebuilder)"

