#: src/getting-started.md:1
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "入门"

#: src/getting-started.md:3
msgid "This guide creates a sample project to show you how it works. This sample:"
msgstr "本指南创建一个示例项目以演示其工作方式。该示例："

#: src/getting-started.md:5
msgid "Reconcile a Memcached CR - which represents an instance of a Memcached deployed/managed on cluster"
msgstr "对 Memcached CR 进行调整 - 该 CR 表示在集群上部署/管理的 Memcached 实例"

#: src/getting-started.md:6
msgid "Create a Deployment with the Memcached image"
msgstr "使用 Memcached 镜像创建一个部署"

#: src/getting-started.md:7
msgid "Not allow more instances than the size you define in the CR"
msgstr "不允许超过 CR 中定义的 size 的实例数"

#: src/getting-started.md:8
msgid "Update the Memcached CR status"
msgstr "更新 Memcached CR 状态"

#: src/getting-started.md:13
msgid "By following the [Operator Pattern](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/extend-kubernetes/operator/), it’s possible not only to provide all expected resources but also to manage them dynamically, programmatically, and at execution time. To illustrate this idea, imagine if someone accidentally changed a configuration or removed a resource by mistake; in this case, the operator could fix it without any human intervention."
msgstr "通过遵循 [ Operator 模式](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/extend-kubernetes/operator/)，不仅可以提供所有预期的资源，还可以动态地、以编程的方式和在执行时对其进行管理。为了说明这个想法，设想一下如果有人意外更改了配置或错误地移除了某个资源；在这种情况下，Operator 可以在没有任何人工干预的情况下进行修复。"

#: src/getting-started.md:23
msgid "Note that most of this tutorial is generated from literate Go files that form a runnable project, and live in the book source directory: [docs/book/src/getting-started/testdata/project](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/tree/master/docs/book/src/cronjob-tutorial/testdata/project)."
msgstr "请注意，本教程的大部分内容是从可运行项目的文档化 Go 文件生成的，这些文件位于书籍源代码目录中：[docs/book/src/getting-started/testdata/project](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/tree/master/docs/book/src/cronjob-tutorial/testdata/project)。"

#: src/getting-started.md:31
msgid "First, create and navigate into a directory for your project. Then, initialize it using `kubebuilder`:"
msgstr "首先，创建并导航到你的项目目录。然后，使用 `kubebuilder` 初始化它："

#: src/getting-started.md:42 src/cronjob-tutorial/cronjob-tutorial.md:65
msgid "If you initialize your project within [`GOPATH`](https://golang.org/doc/code.html#GOPATH), the implicitly called `go mod init` will interpolate the module path for you. Otherwise `--repo=<module path>` must be set."
msgstr "若在 [`GOPATH`](https://golang.org/doc/code.html#GOPATH) 内初始化项目，隐式调用的 `go mod init` 会为您推导模块路径。否则必须设置 `--repo=<module path>`。"

#: src/getting-started.md:45 src/cronjob-tutorial/cronjob-tutorial.md:68
msgid "Read the [Go modules blogpost](https://blog.golang.org/using-go-modules) if unfamiliar with the module system."
msgstr "如果对模块系统不熟悉，请阅读 [Go模块博客](https://blog.golang.org/using-go-modules)。"

#: src/getting-started.md:49
msgid "Create the Memcached API (CRD)"
msgstr "创建 Memcached API（CRD）"

#: src/getting-started.md:51
msgid "Next, create the API which is responsible for deploying and managing Memcached(s) instances on the cluster."
msgstr "接下来，创建负责在集群上部署并管理 Memcached 实例的 API。"

#: src/getting-started.md:58
msgid "Understanding APIs"
msgstr "理解API"

#: src/getting-started.md:60
msgid "This command's primary aim is to produce the Custom Resource (CR) and Custom Resource Definition (CRD) for the Memcached Kind. It creates the API with the group `cache.example.com` and version `v1alpha1`, uniquely identifying the new CRD of the Memcached Kind. By leveraging the Kubebuilder tool, you can define your APIs and objects representing your solutions for these platforms."
msgstr "该命令的主要目的是为 Memcached Kind 生成自定义资源（CR）与自定义资源定义（CRD）。它创建 group 为 `cache.example.com`、version 为 `v1alpha1` 的 API，唯一标识 Memcached Kind 的新 CRD。借助 Kubebuilder，您可以定义代表这些平台上解决方案的 API 与对象。"

#: src/getting-started.md:64
msgid "While this example adds only one Kind of resource, you can have as many `Groups` and `Kinds` as necessary. To make it easier to understand, think of CRDs as the definition of our custom Objects, while CRs are instances of them."
msgstr "本示例只添加一种 Kind 资源，但您可以按需拥有任意数量的 `Groups` 与 `Kinds`。为便于理解，可将 CRD 视为自定义对象的定义，而 CR 是它们的实例。"

#: src/getting-started.md:70
msgid "[Groups and Versions and Kinds, oh my!](./cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md)."
msgstr "[组、版本和种类，真是让人头大！](./cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md)。"

