#: src/getting-started.md:406
msgid "Reconciliation process"
msgstr "协调过程"

#: src/getting-started.md:408
msgid "In a simplified way, Kubernetes works by allowing you to declare the desired state of your system, and then its controllers continuously observe the cluster and take actions to ensure that the actual state matches the desired state. For your custom APIs and controllers, the process is similar. Remember, you are extending Kubernetes' behaviors and its APIs to fit your specific needs."
msgstr "简单来说，Kubernetes 允许声明系统期望状态，控制器持续观察集群并采取行动，使实际状态与期望状态一致。自定义 API 与控制器的过程类似。请记住，您是在扩展 Kubernetes 行为及其 API 以满足特定需求。"

#: src/getting-started.md:410
msgid "In our controller, we implement a reconciliation process."
msgstr "在控制器中，我们实现协调过程。"

#: src/getting-started.md:412
msgid "Essentially, the reconciliation process functions as a loop, continuously checking conditions and performing necessary actions until the desired state is achieved. This process will keep running until all conditions in the system align with the desired state defined in our implementation."
msgstr "本质上， reconciliation 过程作为一个循环运行，不断检查条件并执行必要的操作，直到达到所需的状态。该过程将持续运行，直到系统中的所有条件与我们实施中定义的所需状态一致。"

#: src/getting-started.md:414
msgid "Here's a pseudo-code example to illustrate this:"
msgstr "这是一个伪代码示例来说明这一点："

#: src/getting-started.md:419
msgid ""
"// Check if a Deployment for the app exists, if not, create one\n"
"  // If there is an error, then restart from the beginning of the reconcile\n"
msgstr ""
"// 检查应用的 Deployment 是否存在，若不存在则创建\n"
"  // 若出错，则从协调过程开头重新开始\n"

#: src/getting-started.md:425
msgid ""
"// Check if a Service for the app exists, if not, create one\n"
"  // If there is an error, then restart from the beginning of the reconcile\n"
msgstr ""
"// 检查应用的 Service 是否存在，若不存在则创建\n"
"  // 若出错，则从协调过程开头重新开始\n"

#: src/getting-started.md:431
msgid ""
"// Look for Database CR/CRD\n"
"  // Check the Database Deployment's replicas size\n"
"  // If deployment.replicas size does not match cr.size, then update it\n"
"  // Then, requeue the reconciliation to ensure the desired state is reached. For example, by returning `reconcile.Result{RequeueAfter: time.Minute}, nil`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 查找 Database CR/CRD\n"
"  // 检查 Database Deployment 的副本数\n"
"  // 若 deployment.replicas 与 cr.size 不匹配， then update it\n"
"  // Then, requeue the reconciliation to ensure the desired state is reached. For example, by returning `reconcile.Result{RequeueAfter: time.Minute}, nil`.\n"

#: src/getting-started.md:440
msgid ""
"// If at the end of the loop:\n"
"  // Everything executed successfully, and the reconcile can stop\n"
msgstr ""
"// 若循环结束时：\n"
"  // 全部执行成功，协调可以停止\n"

#: src/getting-started.md:450
msgid "The following are a few possible return options to restart the Reconcile:"
msgstr "以下是一些可能的返回选项，用于重新启动对账："

#: src/getting-started.md:452
msgid "With the error:"
msgstr "出现错误："

#: src/getting-started.md:457
msgid "Without an error (requeue after a delay):"
msgstr "无错误（延迟后重新入队）："

#: src/getting-started.md:463
msgid "Reconcile again after a computed duration:"
msgstr "在计算的时长后再次协调："

#: src/getting-started.md:471
msgid "In the context of our example"
msgstr "在我们例子的背景下。"

#: src/getting-started.md:473
msgid "When you apply the sample Custom Resource (CR) to the cluster (i.e. `kubectl apply -f config/sample/cache_v1alpha1_memcached.yaml`), ensure that the controller creates a Deployment for the Memcached image and that it matches the number of replicas you define in the CR."
msgstr "将示例自定义资源（CR）应用到集群时（即 `kubectl apply -f config/sample/cache_v1alpha1_memcached.yaml`），确保控制器为 Memcached 镜像创建 Deployment，且副本数与 CR 中定义一致。"

#: src/getting-started.md:476
msgid "To achieve this, first implement an operation that checks whether the Deployment for the Memcached instance already exists on the cluster. If it does not, the controller creates the Deployment accordingly. Therefore, our reconciliation process must include an operation to ensure that this desired state is consistently maintained. This operation would involve:"
msgstr "为此，首先实现检查集群上是否已有该 Memcached 实例的 Deployment 的操作；若不存在，控制器再创建。因此协调过程必须包含用于持续维持该期望状态的操作，例如："

