#: src/getting-started.md:831
msgid "Diving into the controller implementation"
msgstr "深入控制器实现"

#: src/getting-started.md:833
msgid "Setting manager to watching resources"
msgstr "配置 Manager 监视资源"

#: src/getting-started.md:835
msgid "The whole idea is to be Watching the resources that matter for the controller. When a resource that the controller is interested in changes, the Watch triggers the controller's reconciliation loop, ensuring that the actual state of the resource matches the desired state as defined in the controller's logic."
msgstr "整个想法是关注对控制器重要的资源。当控制器感兴趣的资源发生变化时，Watch 会触发控制器的对账循环，确保资源的实际状态与控制器逻辑中定义的期望状态相匹配。"

#: src/getting-started.md:840
msgid "Notice how you configure the Manager to monitor events such as the creation, update, or deletion of a Custom Resource (CR) of the Memcached kind, as well as any changes to the Deployment that the controller manages and owns:"
msgstr "注意如何配置 Manager，以监视 Memcached Kind 自定义资源（CR）的创建、更新或删除，以及控制器所管理并拥有的 Deployment 的任何变更："

#: src/getting-started.md:844
msgid ""
"// SetupWithManager sets up the controller with the Manager.\n"
"// The Deployment is also watched to ensure its\n"
"// desired state in the cluster.\n"
msgstr ""
"// SetupWithManager 将控制器与管理器设置起来。\n"
"// 部署也会被监视以确保其\n"
"// 在集群中的期望状态。\n"

#: src/getting-started.md:849
msgid ""
"// Watch the Memcached Custom Resource and trigger reconciliation whenever it\n"
"\t\t//when you create, update, or delete it\n"
msgstr ""
"// 监视 Memcached 自定义资源，并在其\n"
"\t\t//创建、更新或删除时触发协调\n"

#: src/getting-started.md:852
msgid ""
"// Watch the Deployment managed by the Memcached controller. If any changes occur to the Deployment\n"
"        // owned and managed by this controller, it triggers reconciliation, ensuring that the cluster\n"
"        // state aligns with the desired state.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 监视由 Memcached 控制器管理的 Deployment。若 Deployment 发生任何变更\n"
"        // owned and managed by this controller, it triggers reconciliation, ensuring that the cluster\n"
"        // state aligns with the desired state.\n"

#: src/getting-started.md:860
msgid "But, how does the manager know which resources are owned by it?"
msgstr "但是，Manager 如何知道哪些资源归它所有？"

#: src/getting-started.md:862
msgid "The Controller should not watch any Deployment on the cluster and trigger the reconciliation loop. Instead, trigger reconciliation only when the specific Deployment running the Memcached instance is changed. For example, if someone accidentally deletes the Deployment or changes the number of replicas, trigger the reconciliation to ensure that it returns to the desired state."
msgstr "控制器不应监视集群上任意 Deployment 并触发协调循环，而应仅在运行 Memcached 实例的特定 Deployment 发生变化时触发。例如，若有人误删 Deployment 或更改副本数，应触发协调以恢复期望状态。"

#: src/getting-started.md:868
msgid "The Manager knows which Deployment to observe because you set the `ownerRef` (Owner Reference):"
msgstr "Manager 知道应观察哪个 Deployment，是因为设置了 `ownerRef`（所有者引用）："

#: src/getting-started.md:880
msgid "The ownerRef is crucial not only for allowing the controller to observe changes on the specific resource but also because, if you delete the Memcached Custom Resource (CR) from the cluster, all resources owned by it are automatically deleted as well, in a cascading event."
msgstr "ownerRef 至关重要：它不仅让控制器观察特定资源的变更，而且当从集群删除 Memcached 自定义资源（CR）时，其拥有的全部资源也会在级联事件中被自动删除。"

#: src/getting-started.md:884
msgid "This ensures that when you remove the parent resource (Memcached CR), Kubernetes also removes all associated resources (like Deployments, Services, etc.) are also cleaned up, maintaining a tidy and consistent cluster state."
msgstr "这确保删除父资源（Memcached CR）时，Kubernetes 也会清理所有关联资源（如 Deployment、Service 等），保持集群整洁一致。"

#: src/getting-started.md:888
msgid "For more information, see the Kubernetes documentation on [Owners and Dependents](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/owners-dependents/)."
msgstr "有关更多信息，请参阅 Kubernetes 文档中的 [拥有者和依赖项](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/owners-dependents/)。"

#: src/getting-started.md:892
msgid "Granting permissions"
msgstr "授予权限"

#: src/getting-started.md:894
msgid "It's important to ensure that the Controller has the necessary permissions (i.e., to create, get, update, and list) the resources it manages."
msgstr "务必确保控制器对其管理的资源具备必要权限（例如 create、get、update、list）。"

#: src/getting-started.md:897
msgid "You configure the [RBAC permissions](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/rbac/) via [RBAC markers](./reference/markers/rbac.md), which [controller-gen](./reference/controller-gen.md) uses to generate and update the manifest files in `config/rbac/`. You can find these markers (and should define them) on the `Reconcile()` method of each controller, see how the example implements them:"
msgstr "通过 [RBAC 标记](./reference/markers/rbac.md) 配置 [RBAC 权限](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/rbac/)，[controller-gen](./reference/controller-gen.md) 据此生成并更新 `config/rbac/` 中的清单。可在各控制器的 `Reconcile()` 方法上找到（并应定义）这些标记，参见示例实现："

#: src/getting-started.md:910
msgid "After making changes to the controller, run the make manifests command. This will prompt [controller-gen](./reference/controller-gen.md) to refresh the files located under `config/rbac`."
msgstr "修改控制器后，运行 make manifests。这将让 [controller-gen](./reference/controller-gen.md) 刷新 `config/rbac` 下的文件。"

