#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:1
msgid "Groups and versions and kinds, oh my!"
msgstr "组、版本和种类，真是让人头大！"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:3
msgid "Before getting started with the API, talk about terminology a bit."
msgstr "开始 API 之前，先谈一点术语。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:6
msgid "When discussing APIs in Kubernetes, 4 terms are often used: _groups_, _versions_, _kinds_, and _resources_."
msgstr "讨论 Kubernetes API 时常用四个术语：_groups_（组）、_versions_（版本）、_kinds_（种类）和 _resources_（资源）。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:9
msgid "Groups and versions"
msgstr "组与版本"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:11
msgid "An _API Group_ in Kubernetes is simply a collection of related functionality.  Each group has one or more _versions_, which, as the name suggests, allow you to change how an API works over time."
msgstr "Kubernetes 中的 _API 组_ 只是相关功能的集合。每个组都有一个或多个 _版本_，顾名思义，这些版本允许我们随着时间的推移改变 API 的工作方式。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:15
msgid "Kinds and resources"
msgstr "种类与资源"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:17
msgid "Each API group-version contains one or more API types, called _Kinds_.  While a Kind may change forms between versions, each form must be able to store all the data of the other forms, somehow (you can store the data in fields, or in annotations).  This means that using an older API version will not cause newer data to be lost or corrupted.  See the [Kubernetes API guidelines](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md) for more information."
msgstr "每个 API 组版本包含一个或多个 API 类型，我们称之为 _Kinds_。虽然一个 Kind 可能在不同版本之间改变形式，但每种形式必须能够以某种方式存储其他形式的所有数据（我们可以将数据存储在字段中或注释中）。这意味着使用旧的 API 版本不会导致较新的数据丢失或损坏。有关更多信息，请参阅 [Kubernetes API 指南](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md)。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:26
msgid "You'll also hear mention of _resources_ on occasion.  A resource is simply a use of a Kind in the API.  Often, there is a one-to-one mapping between Kinds and resources.  For instance, the `pods` resource corresponds to the `Pod` Kind.  However, sometimes, the same Kind may be returned by multiple resources.  For instance, the `Scale` Kind is returned by all scale subresources, like `deployments/scale` or `replicasets/scale`.  This is what allows the Kubernetes HorizontalPodAutoscaler to interact with different resources.  With CRDs, however, each Kind will correspond to a single resource."
msgstr "您有时还会听到提到 _资源_。资源只是 API 中对 Kind 的一种使用。通常，Kinds 和资源之间存在一对一的映射关系。例如，`pods` 资源对应于 `Pod` Kind。然而，有时候，同一个 Kind 可能会由多个资源返回。例如，`Scale` Kind 会由所有缩放子资源返回，如 `deployments/scale` 或 `replicasets/scale`。这使得 Kubernetes 的 HorizontalPodAutoscaler 能够与不同的资源进行交互。然而，对于自定义资源定义（CRDs）而言，每个 Kind 将对应一个单一的资源。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:36
msgid "Notice that resources are always lowercase, and by convention are the lowercase form of the Kind."
msgstr "请注意，资源始终使用小写字母，并且根据惯例，它们是 Kind 的小写形式。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:39
msgid "So, how does that correspond to Go?"
msgstr "那么，这与围棋有什么关系呢？"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:41
msgid "When referring to a kind in a particular group version, it is called a _GroupVersionKind_, or GVK for short.  Same with resources and GVR. As you'll see shortly, each GVK corresponds to a given root Go type in a package."
msgstr "指称某一特定组版本中的 kind 时，称为 _GroupVersionKind_，简称 GVK。资源对应有 GVR。稍后可见，每个 GVK 对应包中某个根 Go 类型。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:46
msgid "Now that the terminology is clear, _actually_ create the API!"
msgstr "术语清楚后，_真正_ 创建 API！"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:49
msgid "So, how can you create an API?"
msgstr "那么，如何创建 API？"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:51
msgid "In the next section, [Adding a new API](../cronjob-tutorial/new-api.html), check how the tool helps you create your APIs with the command `kubebuilder create api`."
msgstr "在下一部分[添加新的 API](../cronjob-tutorial/new-api.html)中，我们将检查该工具如何通过命令 `kubebuilder create api` 帮助我们创建自己的 API。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:54
msgid "The goal of this command is to create a Custom Resource (CR) and Custom Resource Definition (CRD) for your Kind(s). To check it further see; [Extend the Kubernetes API with CustomResourceDefinitions](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/custom-resources/custom-resource-definitions/)."
msgstr "此命令的目标是为我们的类型创建一个自定义资源（CR）和自定义资源定义（CRD）。要进一步了解，请参见：[使用自定义资源定义扩展Kubernetes API](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/custom-resources/custom-resource-definitions/)。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:56
msgid "But, why create APIs at all?"
msgstr "但是，为什么要创建API呢？"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:58
msgid "New APIs are how you teach Kubernetes about your custom objects. Controller-gen uses the Go structs to generate a CRD which includes the schema for your data as well as tracking data like what the new type is called. You can then create instances of your custom objects which your [controllers](../cronjob-tutorial/controller-overview.md) manage."
msgstr "新 API 是你向 Kubernetes 介绍自定义对象的方式。Controller-gen 用 Go 结构体生成 CRD，其中包含数据 schema 以及新类型名称等跟踪信息。随后可创建由[控制器](../cronjob-tutorial/controller-overview.md)管理的自定义对象实例。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:60
msgid "Your APIs and resources represent your solutions on the clusters. Basically, the CRDs are a definition of your customized Objects, and the CRs are an instance of it."
msgstr "API 与资源代表你在集群上的方案。简单说，CRD 是自定义对象的定义，CR 是其实例。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:62
msgid "Ah, do you have an example?"
msgstr "啊，你有例子吗？"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:64
msgid "Think about the classic scenario where the goal is to have an application and its database running on the platform with Kubernetes. Then, one CRD could represent the App, and another one could represent the DB. By having one CRD to describe the App and another one for the DB, you avoid hurting concepts such as encapsulation, the single responsibility principle, and cohesion. Damaging these concepts could cause unexpected side effects, such as difficulty in extending, reuse, or maintenance, just to mention a few."
msgstr "想想经典场景：目标是在 Kubernetes 平台上运行应用及其数据库。可用一个 CRD 表示 App，另一个表示 DB。分别描述 App 与 DB 可避免破坏封装、单一职责与内聚等概念；损害这些概念可能导致难以扩展、复用或维护等副作用。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:66
msgid "In this way, you can create the App CRD which has its controller and which would be responsible for things like creating Deployments that contain the App and creating Services to access it and etc. Similarly, you could create a CRD to represent the DB, and deploy a controller that would manage DB instances."
msgstr "通过这种方式，我们可以创建应用程序的 CRD，它将拥有自己的控制器，负责诸如创建包含应用程序的 Deployment、创建访问该应用程序的 Service 等。类似地，我们可以创建一个 CRD 来表示数据库，并部署一个控制器来管理数据库实例。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:68
msgid "Err, but what is that Scheme thing?"
msgstr "呃，那个 Scheme 是什么？"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:70
msgid "The `Scheme` you saw before is simply a way to keep track of what Go type corresponds to a given GVK (do not be overwhelmed by its [godocs](https://pkg.go.dev/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/runtime?tab=doc#Scheme))."
msgstr "我们之前看到的 `Scheme` 只是一个用来跟踪给定 GVK 对应的 Go 类型的方式（不要被它的 [godocs](https://pkg.go.dev/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/runtime?tab=doc#Scheme) 压倒）。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:74
msgid "For instance, suppose you mark the `\"tutorial.kubebuilder.io/api/v1\".CronJob{}` type as being in the `batch.tutorial.kubebuilder.io/v1` API group (implicitly saying it has the Kind `CronJob`)."
msgstr "例如，假设我们将 `\"tutorial.kubebuilder.io/api/v1\".CronJob{}` 类型标记为属于 `batch.tutorial.kubebuilder.io/v1` API 组（隐含地表示它的 Kind 为 `CronJob`）。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:79
msgid "Then, you can later construct a new `&CronJob{}` given some JSON from the API server that says"
msgstr "然后，我们可以根据API服务器提供的JSON数据，稍后构建一个新的 `&CronJob{}`。"

