#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:3
msgid "To scaffold out a new Kind (you were paying attention to the [last chapter](./gvks.md#kinds-and-resources), right?) and corresponding controller, use `kubebuilder create api`:"
msgstr "要构建一个新的 Kind（你有注意到[上一章](./gvks.md#kinds-and-resources)吗？），以及相应的控制器，我们可以使用 `kubebuilder create api`："

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:11
msgid "Press `y` for \"Create Resource\" and \"Create Controller\"."
msgstr "按 `y` 以确认\\"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:13
msgid "The first time you call this command for each group-version, it creates a directory for the new group-version."
msgstr "第一次为每个组版本调用此命令时，它将为新的组版本创建一个目录。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:16
msgid "In this case, the command creates the [`api/v1/`](https://sigs.k8s.io/kubebuilder/docs/book/src/cronjob-tutorial/testdata/project/api/v1) directory, corresponding to the `batch.tutorial.kubebuilder.io/v1` (remember our [`--domain` setting](cronjob-tutorial.md#scaffolding-out-our-project) from the beginning?)."
msgstr "在这种情况下，[`api/v1/`](https://sigs.k8s.io/kubebuilder/docs/book/src/cronjob-tutorial/testdata/project/api/v1) 目录被创建，对应于 `batch.tutorial.kubebuilder.io/v1`（还记得我们最开始的 [`--domain` 设置](cronjob-tutorial.md#scaffolding-out-our-project) 吗？）。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:23
msgid "It has also added a file for the `CronJob` Kind, `api/v1/cronjob_types.go`.  Each time you call the command with a different kind, it adds a corresponding new file."
msgstr "它还为我们的 `CronJob` 类型添加了一个文件 `api/v1/cronjob_types.go`。每次我们调用带有不同类型的命令时，它都会添加一个相应的新文件。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:27
msgid "Take a look at what you have been given out of the box, then move on to filling it out."
msgstr "先看看开箱即得的内容，再动手填写。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:32
#: src/cronjob-tutorial/controller-overview.md:21
msgid "Copyright 2022."
msgstr "Copyright 2022."

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:48
msgid "We start out simply enough: we import the `meta/v1` API group, which is not normally exposed by itself, but instead contains metadata common to all Kubernetes Kinds."
msgstr "开始很简单：导入 `meta/v1` API 组——它通常不单独暴露，而是包含所有 Kubernetes Kind 共用的元数据。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:62
msgid "Next, we define types for the Spec and Status of our Kind.  Kubernetes functions by reconciling desired state (`Spec`) with actual cluster state (other objects' `Status`) and external state, and then recording what it observed (`Status`). Thus, every _functional_ object includes spec and status.  A few types, like `ConfigMap` don't follow this pattern, since they don't encode desired state, but most types do."
msgstr "接下来为 Kind 定义 Spec 与 Status 类型。Kubernetes 通过协调期望状态（`Spec`）与实际集群状态（其他对象的 `Status`）及外部状态，并记录观测结果（`Status`）来工作。因此每个_功能性_对象都包含 spec 与 status。少数类型如 `ConfigMap` 不遵循该模式（它们不编码期望状态），但多数类型如此。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:73 src/cronjob-tutorial/api-design.md:109
#: src/multiversion-tutorial/api-changes.md:93
#: src/multiversion-tutorial/api-changes.md:315
msgid ""
"// CronJobSpec defines the desired state of CronJob\n"
msgstr ""
"// CronJobSpec 定义 CronJob 的期望状态\n"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:79
msgid ""
"// CronJobStatus defines the observed state of CronJob\n"
msgstr ""
"// CronJobStatus 定义 CronJob 的观测状态\n"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:88
msgid "Next, we define the types corresponding to actual Kinds, `CronJob` and `CronJobList`. `CronJob` is our root type, and describes the `CronJob` kind.  Like all Kubernetes objects, it contains `TypeMeta` (which describes API version and Kind), and also contains `ObjectMeta`, which holds things like name, namespace, and labels."
msgstr "接着定义对应实际 Kind 的类型：`CronJob` 与 `CronJobList`。`CronJob` 是根类型，描述 `CronJob` kind。与所有 Kubernetes 对象一样，它包含 `TypeMeta`（描述 API 版本与 Kind）以及 `ObjectMeta`（名称、命名空间、标签等）。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:93
msgid "`CronJobList` is simply a container for multiple `CronJob`s.  It's the Kind used in bulk operations, like LIST."
msgstr "`CronJobList` 只是多个 `CronJob` 的容器，用于 LIST 等批量操作。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:96
msgid "In general, we never modify either of these -- all modifications go in either Spec or Status."
msgstr "通常不会直接修改这两者——所有修改都在 Spec 或 Status 中进行。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:98
msgid "That little `+kubebuilder:object:root` comment is called a marker.  We'll see more of them in a bit, but know that they act as extra metadata, telling [controller-tools](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-tools) (our code and YAML generator) extra information. This particular one tells the `object` generator that this type represents a Kind.  Then, the `object` generator generates an implementation of the [runtime.Object](https://pkg.go.dev/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/runtime?tab=doc#Object) interface for us, which is the standard interface that all types representing Kinds must implement."
msgstr "那个小小的 `+kubebuilder:object:root` 注释叫做标记。稍后会见到更多；它们是额外元数据，告诉 [controller-tools](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-tools)（代码与 YAML 生成器）更多信息。这一条告诉 `object` 生成器该类型表示一个 Kind，于是生成器为我们实现 [runtime.Object](https://pkg.go.dev/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/runtime?tab=doc#Object) 接口——所有表示 Kind 的类型都必须实现它。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:110 src/cronjob-tutorial/api-design.md:236
msgid ""
"// CronJob is the Schema for the cronjobs API\n"
msgstr ""
"// CronJob 是 cronjobs API 的 Schema\n"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:121 src/cronjob-tutorial/api-design.md:259
#: src/multiversion-tutorial/api-changes.md:257
#: src/multiversion-tutorial/api-changes.md:453
msgid ""
"// CronJobList contains a list of CronJob\n"
msgstr ""
"// CronJobList 包含一个 CronJob 列表\n"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:131
msgid "Finally, we add the Go types to the API group.  This allows us to add the types in this API group to any [Scheme](https://pkg.go.dev/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/runtime?tab=doc#Scheme)."
msgstr "最后把 Go 类型加入 API 组，以便把该组中的类型加入任意 [Scheme](https://pkg.go.dev/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/runtime?tab=doc#Scheme)。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/new-api.md:142
msgid "Now that you have seen the basic structure, fill it out!"
msgstr "现在我们已经了解了基本结构，让我们来完善它吧！"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/api-design.md:3
msgid "In Kubernetes, there are a few rules for how you design APIs. Namely, all serialized fields _must_ be `camelCase`, so use JSON struct tags to specify this.  You can also use the `omitempty` struct tag to mark that a field should be omitted from serialization when empty."
msgstr "在 Kubernetes 中设计 API 有若干规则。即：所有序列化字段_必须_为 `camelCase`，因此用 JSON 结构体标签指定。也可用 `omitempty` 标记空值时省略序列化。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/api-design.md:8
msgid "Fields may use most of the primitive types.  Numbers are the exception: for API compatibility purposes, accept three forms of numbers: `int32` and `int64` for integers, and `resource.Quantity` for decimals."
msgstr "字段可以使用大部分原始类型。数字是一个例外：出于API兼容性考虑，我们接受三种数字形式：`int32` 和 `int64` 用于整数，`resource.Quantity` 用于小数。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/api-design.md:14
msgid "Quantities are a special notation for decimal numbers that have an explicitly fixed representation that makes them more portable across machines.  You've probably noticed them when specifying resources requests and limits on pods in Kubernetes."
msgstr "数量是对十进制数字的一种特殊表示法，它具有明确固定的表示方式，使其在不同机器之间更具可移植性。您可能在Kubernetes中为pod指定资源请求和限制时注意到了它们。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/api-design.md:19
msgid "They conceptually work similar to floating point numbers: they have a significant, base, and exponent. Their serializable and human readable format uses whole numbers and suffixes to specify values much the way you would describe computer storage."
msgstr "它们在概念上与浮点数相似：具有有效数字、基数和指数。它们的可序列化和可读格式使用整数和后缀来指定值，方式与我们描述计算机存储的方式类似。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/api-design.md:24
msgid "For instance, the value `2m` means `0.002` in decimal notation.  `2Ki` means `2048` in decimal, while `2K` means `2000` in decimal.  To specify fractions, switch to a suffix that lets you use a whole number: `2.5` is `2500m`."
msgstr "例如，值 `2m` 在十进制表示中代表 `0.002`。 `2Ki` 在十进制中表示 `2048`，而 `2K` 在十进制中表示 `2000`。如果我们想指定小数，我们可以切换到一个后缀，使我们能够使用整数：`2.5` 表示为 `2500m`。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/api-design.md:29
msgid "There are two supported bases: 10 and 2 (called decimal and binary, respectively).  Decimal base is indicated with \"normal\" SI suffixes (e.g. `M` and `K`), while Binary base is specified in \"mebi\" notation (e.g. `Mi` and `Ki`).  Think [megabytes vs mebibytes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binary_prefix)."
msgstr "支持两种进制：10 进制和 2 进制（分别称为十进制和二进制）。十进制使用\"常规\"国际单位制后缀表示（例如 `M` 和 `K`），而二进制使用\"兆比特\"（mebi）表示法（例如 `Mi` 和 `Ki`）。可以参考 [兆字节与兆比特](https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E5%85%83%E7%B4%A0%E9%87%8A%E8%A7%A3) 的区别。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/api-design.md:37
msgid "There is one other special type to use: `metav1.Time`.  This functions identically to `time.Time`, except that it has a fixed, portable serialization format."
msgstr "我们使用的另一种特殊类型是 `metav1.Time`。它的功能与 `time.Time` 相同，但具有固定的可移植序列化格式。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/api-design.md:41
msgid "With that out of the way, take a look at what the CronJob object looks like!"
msgstr "在处理完这些之后，我们来看看我们的 CronJob 对象是什么样的！"

