#: src/cronjob-tutorial/controller-overview.md:95
msgid "`Reconcile` actually performs the reconciling for a single named object. Our [Request](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/reconcile?tab=doc#Request) just has a name, but we can use the client to fetch that object from the cache."
msgstr "`Reconcile` 实际对单个具名对象执行协调。我们的 [Request](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/reconcile?tab=doc#Request) 只有名称，但可用 client 从缓存获取该对象。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/controller-overview.md:99
msgid "We return an empty result and no error, which indicates to controller-runtime that we've successfully reconciled this object and don't need to try again until there's some changes."
msgstr "我们返回空结果且无错误，这向 controller-runtime 表明已成功协调该对象，在出现变更前无需重试。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/controller-overview.md:103
msgid "Most controllers need a logging handle and a context, so we set them up here."
msgstr "多数控制器需要日志句柄与 context，因此在此设置。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/controller-overview.md:105
msgid "The [context](https://golang.org/pkg/context/) is used to allow cancellation of requests, and potentially things like tracing.  It's the first argument to all client methods.  The `Background` context is just a basic context without any extra data or timing restrictions."
msgstr "[context](https://golang.org/pkg/context/) 用于允许取消请求，以及可能的追踪等。它是所有客户端方法的第一个参数。`Background` context 只是没有额外数据或时间限制的基本 context。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/controller-overview.md:110
msgid "The logging handle lets us log.  controller-runtime uses structured logging through a library called [logr](https://github.com/go-logr/logr).  As we'll see shortly, logging works by attaching key-value pairs to a static message.  We can pre-assign some pairs at the top of our reconcile method to have those attached to all log lines in this reconciler."
msgstr "日志句柄让我们记录日志。controller-runtime 通过名为 [logr](https://github.com/go-logr/logr) 的库使用结构化日志。稍后会看到，日志通过向静态消息附加键值对工作。我们可以在 reconcile 方法顶部预分配一些键值对，使它们附加到此 reconciler 的所有日志行。"

