#: src/multiversion-tutorial/api-changes.md:15
msgid "Make it a bit more structured.  According to the [CronJob code](./multiversion-tutorial/testdata/project/api/v2/cronjob_types.go \"CronJob Code\"), it supports \"standard\" Cron format."
msgstr "让它更结构化一些。根据 [CronJob 代码](./multiversion-tutorial/testdata/project/api/v2/cronjob_types.go \"CronJob Code\")，它支持「标准」Cron 格式。"

#: src/multiversion-tutorial/api-changes.md:18
msgid "In Kubernetes, **all versions must be safely round-tripable through each other**.  This means that if you convert from version 1 to version 2, and then back to version 1, you must not lose information.  Thus, any change you make to your API must be compatible with whatever you supported in v1, and you also need to make sure anything you add in v2 is supported in v1.  In some cases, this means you need to add new fields to v1, but in this case, you will not have to, since you are not adding new functionality."
msgstr "在 Kubernetes 中，**所有版本必须能安全地相互往返转换**。这意味着若从版本 1 转到版本 2，再转回版本 1，不得丢失信息。因此，对 API 的任何变更都必须与 v1 所支持的内容兼容，并且要确保在 v2 添加的任何内容在 v1 中也受支持。有时这意味着需要向 v1 添加新字段，但本例不必，因为你没有添加新功能。"

#: src/multiversion-tutorial/api-changes.md:26
msgid "Keeping all that in mind, convert the example above to be slightly more structured:"
msgstr "考虑到这些，让我们将上述示例稍微结构化一下："

