msgstr "将事件记录器传递给控制器"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:82
msgid "Events are published from a Controller using an \\[EventRecorder\\]`type CorrelatorOptions struct`, which can be created for a Controller by calling `GetEventRecorder(name string)` on a Manager. See that we change the implementation scaffolded in `cmd/main.go`:"
msgstr "事件是通过控制器使用`\\[EventRecorder\\]`类型的CorrelatorOptions结构发布的，可以通过在管理器上调用`GetRecorder(name string)`为控制器创建。请注意，我们将更改在`cmd/main.go`中搭建的实现。"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:97
msgid "Granting the required permissions"
msgstr "授予所需的权限"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:99
msgid "You must also grant the RBAC rules permissions to allow your project to create Events. Therefore, ensure that you add the [RBAC](./markers/rbac.md) into your controller:"
msgstr "您还必须授予 RBAC 规则权限，以允许您的项目创建事件。因此，请确保将 [RBAC](./markers/rbac.md) 添加到您的控制器中："

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:102
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=events.k8s.io,resources=events,verbs=create;patch\n"
msgstr ""
"// +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=events.k8s.io,resources=events,verbs=create;patch\n"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:108
msgid "And then, run `$ make manifests` to update the rules under `config/rbac/role.yaml`."
msgstr "然后，运行 `$ make manifests` 来更新 `config/rbac/role.yaml` 下的规则。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:1
msgid "Watching resources"
msgstr "观看资源"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:3
msgid "When extending the Kubernetes API, ensure that your solutions behave consistently with Kubernetes itself. For example, consider a `Deployment` resource, which a controller manages. This controller is responsible for responding to changes in the cluster—such as when you create, update, or delete a `Deployment`—by triggering reconciliation to ensure the resource’s state matches the desired state."
msgstr "在扩展 Kubernetes API 时，我们的目标是确保我们的解决方案与 Kubernetes 本身的行为一致。例如，考虑一个由控制器管理的 `Deployment` 资源。这个控制器负责响应集群中的变化——例如，当 `Deployment` 被创建、更新或删除时——通过触发调整以确保资源的状态与期望状态相匹配。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:8
msgid "Similarly, when developing controllers, watch for relevant changes in resources that are crucial to your solution. These changes—whether creations, updates, or deletions—should trigger the reconciliation loop to take appropriate actions and maintain consistency across the cluster."
msgstr "同样，在开发 controller 时，请监视对你的方案至关重要的资源上的相关变更。这些变更——无论是创建、更新还是删除——都应触发对账循环以采取适当操作，并在集群中保持一致性。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:12
msgid "The [controller-runtime](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime) library provides several ways to watch and manage resources."
msgstr "[controller-runtime](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime) 库提供了多种方式来监视和管理资源。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:14
msgid "Primary resources"
msgstr "主要资源"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:16
msgid "The **Primary Resource** is the resource that your controller is responsible for managing. For example, if you create a custom resource definition (CRD) for `MyApp`, the corresponding controller is responsible for managing instances of `MyApp`."
msgstr "**主要资源**是你的控制器负责管理的资源。例如，如果你为 `MyApp` 创建了一个自定义资源定义（CRD），那么相应的控制器负责管理 `MyApp` 的实例。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:20
msgid "In this case, `MyApp` is the **Primary Resource** for that controller, and your controller’s reconciliation loop focuses on ensuring the desired state of these primary resources is maintained."
msgstr "在这种情况下，`MyApp` 是该控制器的 **主资源**，您的控制器的调整循环专注于确保这些主资源的期望状态得以维护。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:23
msgid "When you create a new API using Kubebuilder, the CLI scaffolds the following default code, ensuring that the controller watches all relevant events—such as creations, updates, and deletions—for (`For()`) the new API."
msgstr "当你使用 Kubebuilder 创建一个新的 API 时，以下默认代码会被生成，确保控制器监视所有相关事件——例如创建、更新和删除——以便于新的 API。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:27
msgid "This setup guarantees that the system triggers the reconciliation loop whenever you create, update, or delete an instance of the API:"
msgstr "此设置确保每当你创建、更新或删除 API 实例时，系统都会触发对账循环："

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:31
msgid ""
"// Watches the primary resource (e.g., MyApp) for create, update, delete events\n"
msgstr ""
"// 监视主要资源（例如，MyApp）的创建、更新、删除事件\n"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:39
msgid "Secondary resources"
msgstr "次要资源"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:41
msgid "Your controller will likely also need to manage **Secondary Resources**, which are the resources required on the cluster to support the **Primary Resource**."
msgstr "您的控制器可能还需要管理**辅助资源**，这是集群中支持**主要资源**所需的资源。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:44
msgid "Changes to these **Secondary Resources** can directly impact the **Primary Resource**, so the controller must watch and reconcile these resources accordingly."
msgstr "对这些**次级资源**的更改可能会直接影响**主要资源**，因此控制者必须相应地监控和调整这些资源。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:47
msgid "Which are owned by the controller"
msgstr "由控制者拥有的。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:49
msgid "These **Secondary Resources**, such as `Services`, `ConfigMaps`, or `Deployments`, when `Owned` by the controllers, the specific controller creates and manages them and ties them to the **Primary Resource** via [OwnerReferences](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/owners-dependents/)."
msgstr "这些**辅助资源**，例如 `Services`、`ConfigMaps` 或 `Deployments`，在被控制器**拥有**时，由特定控制器创建和管理，并通过 [OwnerReferences](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/owners-dependents/) 与**主资源**相关联。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:53
msgid "For example, if you have a controller to manage your CR(s) of the Kind `MyApp` on the cluster, which represents your application solution, all resources required to ensure that `MyApp` is up and running with the desired number of instances are **Secondary Resources**. The code responsible for creating, deleting, and updating these resources is part of the `MyApp` Controller. Add the appropriate [OwnerReferences](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/owners-dependents/) using the [controllerutil.SetControllerReference](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/controller/controllerutil#SetOwnerReference) function to indicate that these resources are owned by the same controller responsible for managing `MyApp` instances, which the `MyAppReconciler` reconciles."
msgstr "例如，如果我们在集群中有一个控制器来管理 `MyApp` 类型的自定义资源（CR），这代表了我们的应用解决方案，那么确保 `MyApp` 以所需实例数正常运行所需的所有资源将被称为 **次要资源**。负责创建、删除和更新这些资源的代码将是 `MyApp` 控制器的一部分。我们将使用 [controllerutil.SetControllerReference](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/controller/controllerutil#SetOwnerReference) 函数添加适当的 [OwnerReferences](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/owners-dependents/) 以指示这些资源由相同的控制器所拥有，该控制器负责管理 `MyApp` 实例，这些实例将由 `MyAppReconciler` 进行调整。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:63
msgid "Additionally, if you delete the **Primary Resource**, Kubernetes' garbage collection mechanism ensures that all associated **Secondary Resources** are automatically deleted in a cascading manner."
msgstr "此外，如果删除了**主要资源**，Kubernetes 的垃圾回收机制将确保所有关联的**次要资源**以层级方式自动删除。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:67
msgid "Which are NOT `owned` by the controller"
msgstr "哪些不是由控制器\"拥有\"的？"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:69
msgid "Note that **Secondary Resources** can either be APIs/CRDs defined in your project or in other projects that are relevant to the **Primary Resources**, but which the specific controller is not responsible for creating or managing."
msgstr "请注意，**辅助资源**可以是您项目中定义的 API/CRD，也可以是与 **主要资源** 相关的其他项目中的 API/CRD，但特定控制器并不负责创建或管理这些资源。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:72
msgid "For example, if you have a CRD that represents a backup solution (i.e. `MyBackup`) for your `MyApp`, it might need to watch changes in the `MyApp` resource to trigger reconciliation in `MyBackup` to ensure the desired state. Similarly, `MyApp`'s behavior might also be impacted by CRDs/APIs defined in other projects."
msgstr "例如，如果我们有一个表示备份解决方案（即 `MyBackup`）的自定义资源定义（CRD），用于我们的 `MyApp`，它可能需要监视 `MyApp` 资源的变化，以便在 `MyBackup` 中触发对账，确保达到期望的状态。同样，`MyApp` 的行为也可能受到其他项目中定义的 CRD/API 的影响。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:77
msgid "In both scenarios, these resources are treated as **Secondary Resources**, even if they are not `Owned` (i.e., not created or managed) by the `MyAppController`."
msgstr "在这两种情况下，这些资源都被视为**次级资源**，即使它们不是由`MyAppController`\"拥有\"（即没有被创建或管理）。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:80
msgid "In Kubebuilder, resources that are not defined in the project itself and are not a **Core Type** (those not defined in the Kubernetes API) are called **External Types**."
msgstr "在 Kubebuilder 中，未在项目中定义且不是 **核心类型**（即未在 Kubernetes API 中定义的类型）的资源称为 **外部类型**。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:83
msgid "An **External Type** refers to a resource that is not defined in your project but one that you need to watch and respond to. For example, if **Operator A** manages a `MyApp` CRD for application deployment, and **Operator B** handles backups, **Operator B** can watch the `MyApp` CRD as an external type to trigger backup operations based on changes in `MyApp`."
msgstr "**外部类型**是指在您的项目中未定义但您需要监视和响应的资源。例如，如果**操作员 A**管理一个用于应用程序部署的 `MyApp` CRD，而**操作员 B**处理备份，那么**操作员 B**可以将 `MyApp` CRD 视为外部类型，以便根据 `MyApp` 的变化触发备份操作。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:89
msgid "In this scenario, **Operator B** could define a `BackupConfig` CRD that relies on the state of `MyApp`. By treating `MyApp` as a **Secondary Resource**, **Operator B** can watch and reconcile changes in **Operator A**'s `MyApp`, ensuring that the controller initiates backup processes whenever you update or scale `MyApp`."
msgstr "在此场景中，**Operator B** 可以定义依赖 `MyApp` 状态的 `BackupConfig` CRD。通过将 `MyApp` 视为**次要资源（Secondary Resource）**，**Operator B** 可以监视并对账 **Operator A** 的 `MyApp` 变更，确保你在更新或扩缩 `MyApp` 时 controller 启动备份流程。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:93
msgid "General concept of watching resources"
msgstr "观看资源的一般概念"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:95
msgid "Whether you define a resource within your project or it comes from an external project, the concept of **Primary** and **Secondary Resources** remains the same:"
msgstr "无论资源是在您的项目内定义的还是来自外部项目，**主要资源**和**次要资源**的概念始终是相同的："

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:97
msgid "The **Primary Resource** is the resource the controller is primarily responsible for managing."
msgstr "**主要资源**是控制器主要负责管理的资源。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:98
msgid "**Secondary Resources** are those that you need to ensure the primary resource works as desired."
msgstr "**次级资源**是指为了确保主要资源按预期工作而必需的资源。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:100
msgid "Therefore, regardless of whether your project or another project defined the resource, your controller can watch, reconcile, and manage changes to these resources as needed."
msgstr "因此，无论资源由你的项目还是其他项目定义，你的 controller 都可以按需监视、对账并管理这些资源的变更。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:103
msgid "Why does watching the secondary resources matter?"
msgstr "观看二级资源有什么重要性？"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:105
msgid "When building a Kubernetes controller, it is crucial to not only focus on **Primary Resources** but also to monitor **Secondary Resources**. Failing to track these resources can lead to inconsistencies in your controller's behavior and the overall cluster state."
msgstr "在构建 Kubernetes 控制器时，关注 **主要资源** 是至关重要的，但同样重要的是监控 **次要资源**。未能跟踪这些资源可能导致您的控制器行为和整个集群状态的不一致。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:110
msgid "Secondary resources may not be directly managed by your controller, but changes to these resources can still significantly impact the primary resource and your controller's functionality. Here are the key reasons why it is important to watch them:"
msgstr "次级资源可能并不直接由您的控制器管理，但对这些资源的更改仍然会对主资源和您的控制器的功能产生重大影响。以下是关注这些资源的重要原因："

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:115
msgid "**Ensuring Consistency**:"
msgstr "**确保一致性**："

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:116
msgid "Secondary resources (e.g., child objects or external dependencies) may diverge from their desired state. For instance, a secondary resource may be modified or deleted, causing the system to fall out of sync."
msgstr "二级资源（例如，子对象或外部依赖）可能与其预期状态发生偏离。例如，二级资源可能被修改或删除，从而导致系统不同步。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:118
msgid "Watching secondary resources ensures that any changes are detected immediately, allowing the controller to reconcile and restore the desired state."
msgstr "观察辅助资源确保任何变化都能立即被检测到，这使得控制器能够对账并恢复所需状态。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:121
msgid "**Avoiding Random Self-Healing**:"
msgstr "**避免随机自我修复**："

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:122
msgid "Without watching secondary resources, the controller may \"heal\" itself only upon restart or when specific events trigger. This can cause unpredictable or delayed reactions to issues."
msgstr "在没有查看二级资源的情况下，控制器可能只在重启后或在触发特定事件时\"自我恢复\"。这可能导致对问题的反应不可预测或延迟。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:124
msgid "Monitoring secondary resources ensures that inconsistencies are addressed promptly, rather than waiting for a controller restart or external event to trigger reconciliation."
msgstr "监控二级资源可以确保及时处理不一致性，而不是等待控制器重启或外部事件来触发调整。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:127
msgid "**Effective Lifecycle Management**:"
msgstr "**有效的生命周期管理**:"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:128
msgid "Secondary resources might not be owned by the controller directly, but their state still impacts the behavior of primary resources. Without watching these, you risk leaving orphaned or outdated resources."
msgstr "次要资源可能并不直接由控制者拥有，但它们的状态仍然会影响主要资源的行为。如果不对这些进行监控，就可能导致孤儿资源或过时资源的存在。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:130
msgid "Watching non-owned secondary resources lets the controller respond to lifecycle events (create, update, delete) that might affect the primary resource, ensuring consistent behavior across the system."
msgstr "观看非拥有的二级资源使控制器能够对可能影响主资源的生命周期事件（创建、更新、删除）作出响应，从而确保系统行为的一致性。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:133
msgid "See [Watching Secondary Resources That Are Not Owned](./watching-resources/secondary-resources-not-owned.md#configuration-example) for an example."
msgstr "请参阅[观看未拥有的次级资源](./watching-resources/secondary-resources-not-owned.md#configuration-example)以获取示例。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:135
msgid "Why not use `RequeueAfter X` for all scenarios instead of watching resources?"
msgstr "为什么不在所有场景中都使用 `RequeueAfter X` 而不是监听资源呢？"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:137
msgid "Kubernetes controllers are fundamentally **event-driven**. When creating a controller, the **Reconciliation Loop** is typically triggered by **events** such as `create`, `update`, or `delete` actions on resources. This event-driven approach is more efficient and responsive compared to constantly requeuing or polling resources using `RequeueAfter`. This ensures that the system only takes action when necessary, maintaining both performance and efficiency."
msgstr "Kubernetes 控制器本质上是 **事件驱动** 的。在创建控制器时，**调整循环** 通常是由对资源的 `create`、`update` 或 `delete` 操作等 **事件** 触发的。这种事件驱动的方法相比于不断重新排队或轮询资源使用 `RequeueAfter` 更加高效和响应迅速。这确保了系统只在必要时采取行动，从而保持性能和效率。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:143
msgid "In many cases, **watching resources** is the preferred approach for ensuring Kubernetes resources remain in the desired state. It is more efficient, responsive, and aligns with Kubernetes' event-driven architecture. However, there are scenarios where `RequeueAfter` is appropriate and necessary, particularly for managing external systems that do not emit events or for handling resources that take time to converge, such as long-running processes. Relying solely on `RequeueAfter` for all scenarios can lead to unnecessary overhead and delayed reactions. Therefore, it is essential to prioritize **event-driven reconciliation** by configuring your controller to **watch resources** whenever possible, and reserving `RequeueAfter` for situations where you need periodic checks."
msgstr "在许多情况下，**监视资源**是确保Kubernetes资源保持在所需状态的首选方法。它更高效、更灵敏，并且与Kubernetes的事件驱动架构相一致。然而，在某些场景中，`RequeueAfter`是合适且必要的，特别是在管理不发出事件的外部系统或处理需要时间才能收敛的资源时，例如长时间运行的过程。仅依赖`RequeueAfter`处理所有场景可能导致不必要的开销和反应延迟。因此，至关重要的是优先考虑**事件驱动的调整**，通过在可能的情况下配置控制器以**监视资源**，并将`RequeueAfter`保留用于需要定期检查的情况。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:152
msgid "When `RequeueAfter X` is useful"
msgstr "`RequeueAfter X` 何时有用"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:154
msgid "While `RequeueAfter` is not the primary method for triggering reconciliations, there are specific cases where it is necessary, such as:"
msgstr "虽然 `RequeueAfter` 不是触发调整的主要方法，但在某些特定情况下是必要的，例如："

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:157
msgid "**Observing External Systems**: When working with external resources that do not generate events (e.g., external databases or third-party services), `RequeueAfter` allows the controller to periodically check the status of these resources."
msgstr "**观察外部系统**：在处理不生成事件的外部资源（例如，外部数据库或第三方服务）时，`RequeueAfter` 允许控制器定期检查这些资源的状态。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:160
msgid "**Time-Based Operations**: Some tasks, such as rotating secrets or renewing certificates, must happen at specific intervals. `RequeueAfter` ensures these operations are performed on schedule, even when no other changes occur."
msgstr "**基于时间的操作**：一些任务，例如旋转密钥或更新证书，必须在特定的时间间隔内执行。`RequeueAfter` 确保这些操作按计划进行，即使没有其他更改发生。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:163
msgid "**Handling Errors or Delays**: When managing resources that encounter errors or require time to self-heal, `RequeueAfter` ensures the controller waits for a specified duration before checking the resource’s status again, avoiding constant reconciliation attempts."
msgstr "**处理错误或延迟**：在管理遇到错误或需要时间自我修复的资源时，`RequeueAfter` 确保控制器在再次检查资源状态之前等待指定的时间，从而避免不断尝试进行调整。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:167
msgid "Usage of predicates"
msgstr "谓词的使用"

#: src/reference/watching-resources.md:169
msgid "For more complex use cases, [Predicates](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/predicate) can be used to fine-tune when your controller should trigger reconciliation. Predicates allow you to filter events based on specific conditions, such as changes to particular fields, labels, or annotations, ensuring that your controller only responds to relevant events and operates efficiently."
msgstr "对于更复杂的使用场景，可以使用 [谓词](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/predicate) 来精确调整您的控制器何时应该触发状态同步。谓词允许您根据特定条件筛选事件，例如对特定字段、标签或注释的更改，从而确保您的控制器仅对相关事件做出响应，并高效地运行。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:1
msgid "Watching secondary resources `Owned` by the controller"
msgstr "查看控制器\"拥有\"的二级资源"

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:3
msgid "In Kubernetes controllers, it’s common to manage both **Primary Resources** and **Secondary Resources**. A **Primary Resource** is the main resource that the controller is responsible for, while **Secondary Resources** are created and managed by the controller to support the **Primary Resource**."
msgstr "在 Kubernetes 控制器中，通常会同时管理 **主资源** 和 **次资源**。**主资源** 是控制器负责的主要资源，而 **次资源** 是由控制器创建和管理，以支持 **主资源**。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:8
msgid "This section explains how to manage **Secondary Resources** which are `Owned` by the controller. This example shows how to:"
msgstr "本节说明如何管理由 controller `Owned` 的**次要资源（Secondary Resources）**。本示例展示如何："

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:11
msgid "Set the [Owner Reference](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/controller/controllerutil#SetOwnerReference) between the primary resource (`Busybox`) and the secondary resource (`Deployment`) to ensure proper lifecycle management."
msgstr "在主要资源（`Busybox`）和次要资源（`Deployment`）之间设置[所有者引用](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/controller/controllerutil#SetOwnerReference)，以确保正确的生命周期管理。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:12
msgid "Configure the controller to `Watch` the secondary resource using `Owns()` in `SetupWithManager()`. See that `Deployment` is owned by the `Busybox` controller because it is created and managed by it."
msgstr "将控制器配置为在 `SetupWithManager()` 中使用 `Owns()` 监视次要资源。可以看到 `Deployment` 由 `Busybox` 控制器拥有，因为它将由该控制器创建和管理。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:15
#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:25
msgid "Setting the owner reference"
msgstr "设置拥有者引用"

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:17
msgid "To link the lifecycle of the secondary resource (`Deployment`) to the primary resource (`Busybox`), set an [Owner Reference](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/controller/controllerutil#SetOwnerReference) on the secondary resource. This ensures that Kubernetes automatically handles cascading deletions: if the primary resource is deleted, the secondary resource is also deleted."
msgstr "要将次级资源（`Deployment`）的生命周期与主资源（`Busybox`）连接起来，我们需要在次级资源上设置一个 [所有者引用](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/controller/controllerutil#SetOwnerReference)。这确保了 Kubernetes 会自动处理层叠删除：如果主资源被删除，次级资源也会被删除。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:23
msgid "Controller-runtime provides the [controllerutil.SetControllerReference](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/controller/controllerutil#SetOwnerReference) function, which you can use to set this relationship between the resources."
msgstr "Controller-runtime 提供了 [controllerutil.SetControllerReference](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/controller/controllerutil#SetOwnerReference) 函数，您可以使用它来设置资源之间的关系。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:27
msgid "Below, create the `Deployment` and set the Owner reference between the `Busybox` custom resource and the `Deployment` using `controllerutil.SetControllerReference()`."
msgstr "下面，我们创建 `Deployment` 并使用 `controllerutil.SetControllerReference()` 在 `Busybox` 自定义资源和 `Deployment` 之间设置 Owner 引用。"

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:30
msgid ""
"// deploymentForBusybox returns a Deployment object for Busybox\n"
msgstr ""
"// deploymentForBusybox 返回一个 Busybox 的 Deployment 对象\n"

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:42
#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:46
msgid "\"app\""
msgstr "\"app\""

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:51
msgid "\"busybox\""
msgstr "\"busybox\""

#: src/reference/watching-resources/secondary-owned-resources.md:52
msgid "\"busybox:latest\""
msgstr "\"busybox:latest\""

