#: src/reference/markers.md:1
msgid "Markers for config/code generation"
msgstr "配置/代码生成标记"

#: src/reference/markers.md:3
msgid "Kubebuilder makes use of a tool called [controller-gen](/reference/controller-gen.md) for generating utility code and Kubernetes YAML.  This code and config generation is controlled by the presence of special \"marker comments\" in Go code."
msgstr "Kubebuilder 使用一个名为 [controller-gen](/reference/controller-gen.md) 的工具来生成实用代码和 Kubernetes YAML。此代码和配置的生成是通过在 Go 代码中添加特殊的\"标记注释\"来控制的。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:9
msgid "Markers are single-line comments that start with a plus, followed by a marker name, optionally followed by some marker specific configuration:"
msgstr "标记是以加号开头的单行注释，后面跟着标记名称，后面可以选择性地跟上一些标记特定配置："

#: src/reference/markers.md:13
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Optional\n"
"// +kubebuilder:validation:MaxItems=2\n"
"// +kubebuilder:printcolumn:JSONPath=\".status.replicas\",name=Replicas,type=string\n"
msgstr ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:可选\n"
"// +kubebuilder:validation:最大项数=2\n"
"// +kubebuilder:printcolumn:JSONPath=\".status.replicas\",name=副本数,type=string\n"

#: src/reference/markers.md:21
msgid "Controller-gen supports both (see the output of `controller-gen crd -www`). `+kubebuilder:validation:Optional` and `+optional` can be applied to fields."
msgstr "Controller-gen 支持两者（请查看 `controller-gen crd -www` 的输出）。`+kubebuilder:validation:Optional` 和 `+optional` 可以应用于字段。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:23
msgid "But `+kubebuilder:validation:Optional` can also be applied at the package level such that it applies to every field in the package."
msgstr "但是 `+kubebuilder:validation:Optional` 也可以在包级别应用，这样它就适用于包中的每个字段。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:25
msgid "If you are using controller-gen only then they are redundant, but if you are using other generators or you want developers that need to  build their own clients for your API, you will want to also include `+optional`."
msgstr "如果您仅使用 controller-gen，那么它们是多余的，但如果您使用其他生成器或者您希望开发人员能够为您的 API 构建自己的客户端，则您还需要添加 `+optional`。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:27
msgid "The most reliable way in 1.x to get `+optional` is `omitempty`."
msgstr "在1.x中，获取`+optional`的最可靠方法是使用`omitempty`。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:31
msgid "See each subsection for information about different types of code and YAML generation."
msgstr "请查看每个子部分以获取有关不同类型代码和 YAML 生成的信息。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:34
msgid "Generating code & artifacts in Kubebuilder"
msgstr "在 Kubebuilder 中生成代码和工件"

#: src/reference/markers.md:36
msgid "Kubebuilder projects have two `make` targets that make use of controller-gen:"
msgstr "Kubebuilder 项目有两个 `make` 目标，用于使用 controller-gen："

#: src/reference/markers.md:39
msgid "`make manifests` generates Kubernetes object YAML, like [CustomResourceDefinitions](./markers/crd.md), [WebhookConfigurations](./markers/webhook.md), and [RBAC roles](./markers/rbac.md). When Server-Side Apply is enabled, it also generates [ApplyConfiguration types](./markers/applyconfiguration.md)."
msgstr "`make manifests` 生成 Kubernetes 对象 YAML，如 [CustomResourceDefinitions](./markers/crd.md)、[WebhookConfigurations](./markers/webhook.md) 和 [RBAC roles](./markers/rbac.md)。启用 Server-Side Apply 时，还会生成 [ApplyConfiguration 类型](./markers/applyconfiguration.md)。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:45
msgid "`make generate` generates code, like [runtime.Object/DeepCopy implementations](./markers/object.md)."
msgstr "`make generate` 生成代码，例如 [runtime.Object/DeepCopy 实现](./markers/object.md)。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:48
msgid "See [Generating CRDs](./generating-crd.md) for a comprehensive overview."
msgstr "请查看[生成 CRD](./generating-crd.md)以获取全面概述。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:50
msgid "Marker syntax"
msgstr "标记语法"

#: src/reference/markers.md:52
msgid "Exact syntax is described in the [godocs for controller-tools](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-tools/pkg/markers?tab=doc)."
msgstr "确切的语法在 [controller-tools 的文档](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-tools/pkg/markers?tab=doc) 中进行了描述。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:55
msgid "In general, markers may either be:"
msgstr "通常，标记可以是："

#: src/reference/markers.md:57
msgid "**Empty** (`+kubebuilder:validation:Optional`): empty markers are like boolean flags on the command line \\-- just specifying them enables some behavior."
msgstr "**空** (`+kubebuilder:validation:Optional`): 空标记就像命令行上的布尔标志 \\-- 仅仅指定它们就可以启用某些行为。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:60
msgid "**Anonymous** (`+kubebuilder:validation:MaxItems=2`): anonymous markers take a single value as their argument."
msgstr "**匿名** (`+kubebuilder:validation:MaxItems=2`): 匿名标记的参数只能接受一个值。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:63
msgid "**Multi-option** (`+kubebuilder:printcolumn:JSONPath=\".status.replicas\",name=Replicas,type=string`): multi-option markers take one or more named arguments.  The first argument is separated from the name by a colon, and latter arguments are comma-separated.  Order of arguments does not matter.  Some arguments may be optional."
msgstr "**多选项** (`+kubebuilder:printcolumn:JSONPath=\".status.replicas\",name=Replicas,type=string`): 多选项标记可以接受一个或多个命名参数。 第一个参数通过冒号与名称分隔，后续参数用逗号分隔。 参数的顺序没有关系。 某些参数可能是可选的。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:70
msgid "Marker arguments may be strings, ints, bools, slices, or maps thereof. Strings, ints, and bools follow their Go syntax:"
msgstr "标记参数可以是字符串、整数、布尔值、切片或它们的映射。字符串、整数和布尔值遵循它们的 Go 语法："

#: src/reference/markers.md:74
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:ExclusiveMaximum=false\n"
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Format=\"date-time\"\n"
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Maximum=42\n"
msgstr ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:ExclusiveMaximum=false\n"
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Format=\"date-time\"\n"
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Maximum=42\n"

#: src/reference/markers.md:79
msgid "For convenience, in simple cases the quotes may be omitted from strings, although this is not encouraged for anything other than single-word strings:"
msgstr "为了方便，对于简单情况，可以省略字符串中的引号，但不鼓励在单词字符串以外的其他情况下这样做："

#: src/reference/markers.md:84
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Type=string\n"
msgstr ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Type=string\n"

#: src/reference/markers.md:87
msgid "Slices may be specified either by surrounding them with curly braces and separating with commas:"
msgstr "切片可以通过用大括号包围并用逗号分隔来指定："

#: src/reference/markers.md:91
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:webhooks:Enum={\"crackers, Gromit, we forgot the crackers!\",\"not even wensleydale?\"}\n"
msgstr ""
"// +kubebuilder:webhooks:Enum={\"饼干, 龟兔赛跑, 我们忘记带饼干了!\",\"连温斯莱代尔奶酪都没有吗?\"}\n"

#: src/reference/markers.md:94
msgid "or, in simple cases, by separating with semicolons:"
msgstr "或在简单情况下，用分号分隔："

#: src/reference/markers.md:97
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Enum=Wallace;Gromit;Chicken\n"
msgstr ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Enum=华莱士;格罗米特;鸡\n"

#: src/reference/markers.md:100
msgid "Maps are specified with string keys and values of any type (effectively `map[string]interface{}`). A map is surrounded by curly braces (`{}`), each key and value is separated by a colon (`:`), and each key-value pair is separated by a comma:"
msgstr "映射使用字符串键和任何类型的值指定（实际上是 `map[string]interface{}`）。映射用大括号（`{}`）包围，每个键和值之间用冒号（`:`）分隔，每对键值对之间用逗号分隔："

#: src/reference/markers.md:106
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:default={magic: {numero: 42, stringified: forty-two}}\n"
msgstr ""
"// +kubebuilder:default={magic: {numero: 42, stringified: 四十二}}\n"

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:3
msgid "These markers describe how to construct a custom resource definition from a series of Go types and packages.  Generation of the actual validation schema is described by the [validation markers](./crd-validation.md)."
msgstr "这些标记描述了如何根据一系列 Go 类型和包构建自定义资源定义。实际验证模式的生成由[验证标记](./crd-validation.md)描述。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:7
msgid "See [Generating CRDs](../generating-crd.md) for examples."
msgstr "请参见[生成 CRD](../generating-crd.md)以获取示例。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:11
msgid "This is useful if you need to drop support for a version in favor of a newer version. The version will still be stored in etcd if it's the storage version, but won't be served via the API."
msgstr "若需要放弃某个版本以支持更新版本，这很有用。若该版本是 storage version，仍会存储在 etcd 中，但不会通过 API 提供服务。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:15 src/reference/markers/crd.md:28
#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:42 src/reference/markers/crd.md:72
#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:87 src/reference/markers/crd.md:99
#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:114 src/reference/markers/crd.md:156
#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:194 src/reference/markers/crd.md:226
#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:37
#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:170
#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:182
#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:195
