#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:3
msgid "These markers help control how the Kubernetes API server processes API requests involving your custom resources."
msgstr "这些标记有助于控制 Kubernetes API 服务器如何处理涉及您的自定义资源的 API 请求。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:10
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:42
msgid "i.e. whether each field in the struct is independent of the others, or all fields are treated as a single unit."
msgstr "即 struct 中各字段是否彼此独立，或所有字段视为一个整体。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:13
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:45
msgid "This is important for Server-Side Apply to correctly merge struct updates."
msgstr "这对于 Server-Side Apply 正确合并 struct 更新很重要。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:15
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:47
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:79
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:105
msgid "Possible values:"
msgstr "可能的值："

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:17
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:49
msgid "\"granular\": fields in the struct are independent of each other, and can be manipulated by different actors. This is the default behavior."
msgstr "\"granular\"：结构体中的字段彼此独立，可由不同参与者操作。这是默认行为。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:21
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:53
msgid "\"atomic\": all fields are treated as one unit. Any changes have to replace the entire struct."
msgstr "\"atomic\"：所有字段视为一个整体。任何变更都必须替换整个 struct。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:26
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:58
msgid ""
"    // Granular struct (default) - individual fields can be updated independently\n"
"    // +structType=granular\n"
"    type Config struct {\n"
"        Host string\n"
"        Port int\n"
"    }\n"
"    \n"
"    // Atomic struct - entire struct is replaced on update\n"
"    // +structType=atomic\n"
"    type Credentials struct {\n"
"        Username string\n"
"        Password string\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // Granular struct (default) - individual fields can be updated independently\n"
"    // +structType=granular\n"
"    type Config struct {\n"
"        Host string\n"
"        Port int\n"
"    }\n"
"    \n"
"    // Atomic struct - entire struct is replaced on update\n"
"    // +structType=atomic\n"
"    type Credentials struct {\n"
"        Username string\n"
"        Password string\n"
"    }\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:74
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:100
msgid "i.e. whether each item in the map is independent of the others, or all fields are treated as a single unit."
msgstr "即 map 中各项是否彼此独立，或所有字段视为一个整体。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:77
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:103
msgid "This is important for Server-Side Apply to correctly merge map updates."
msgstr "这对于 Server-Side Apply 正确合并 map 更新很重要。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:81
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:107
msgid "\"granular\": items in the map are independent of each other, and can be manipulated by different actors. This is the default behavior."
msgstr "\"granular\"：map 中的条目彼此独立，可由不同参与者操作。这是默认行为。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:85
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:111
msgid "\"atomic\": all fields are treated as one unit. Any changes have to replace the entire map."
msgstr "\"atomic\"：所有字段视为一个整体。任何变更都必须替换整个 map。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:90
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:116
msgid ""
"    // Granular map (default) - individual keys can be updated independently\n"
"    // +mapType=granular\n"
"    Labels map[string]string\n"
"    \n"
"    // Atomic map - entire map is replaced on update\n"
"    // +mapType=atomic\n"
"    Config map[string]string\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // Granular map (default) - individual keys can be updated independently\n"
"    // +mapType=granular\n"
"    Labels map[string]string\n"
"    \n"
"    // Atomic map - entire map is replaced on update\n"
"    // +mapType=atomic\n"
"    Config map[string]string\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:126
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:159
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:338
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:371
msgid "represents (map, set, atomic)."
msgstr "表示（map、set、atomic）。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:128
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:161
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:340
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:373
msgid "This is important for Server-Side Apply to correctly merge list updates."
msgstr "这对于 Server-Side Apply 正确合并 list 更新很重要。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:130
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:163
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:342
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:375
msgid "Possible data-structure types of a list are:"
msgstr "列表可能的数据结构类型为："

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:132
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:165
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:344
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:377
msgid "\"map\": it needs to have a key field, which will be used to build an associative list. A typical example is a the pod container list, which is indexed by the container name."
msgstr "\"map\"：需要有一个键字段，用于构建关联列表。典型例子是按容器名索引的 pod container 列表。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:136
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:169
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:348
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:381
msgid "\"set\": Fields need to be \"scalar\", and there can be only one occurrence of each."
msgstr "\"set\"：字段需为 \"scalar\"，且每个值只能出现一次。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:139
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:172
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:351
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:384
msgid "\"atomic\": All the fields in the list are treated as a single value, are typically manipulated together by the same actor."
msgstr "\"atomic\"：列表中的所有字段视为单个值，通常由同一参与者一起操作。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:144
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:177
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:356
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:389
msgid ""
"    // Map list (associative list) - items are merged by key\n"
"    // +listType=map\n"
"    // +listMapKey=name\n"
"    Containers []Container\n"
"    \n"
"    // Set list - items must be unique scalars\n"
"    // +listType=set\n"
"    Tags []string\n"
"    \n"
"    // Atomic list - entire list is replaced on update\n"
"    // +listType=atomic\n"
"    Args []string\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // Map list (associative list) - items are merged by key\n"
"    // +listType=map\n"
"    // +listMapKey=name\n"
"    Containers []Container\n"
"    \n"
"    // Set list - items must be unique scalars\n"
"    // +listType=set\n"
"    Tags []string\n"
"    \n"
"    // Atomic list - entire list is replaced on update\n"
"    // +listType=atomic\n"
"    Args []string\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:192
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:211
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:404
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:423
msgid "It indicates the index of a map list. They can be repeated if multiple keys must be used. It can only be used when ListType is set to map, and the keys should be scalar types."
msgstr "它表示 map 列表的索引。若必须使用多个键可以重复。仅当 ListType 设为 map 时可用，且键应为标量类型。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:198
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:217
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:410
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:429
msgid ""
"    // Single key\n"
"    // +listType=map\n"
"    // +listMapKey=name\n"
"    Containers []Container\n"
"    \n"
"    // Composite key (multiple keys)\n"
"    // +listType=map\n"
"    // +listMapKey=name\n"
"    // +listMapKey=protocol\n"
"    Ports []Port\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // Single key\n"
"    // +listType=map\n"
"    // +listMapKey=name\n"
"    Containers []Container\n"
"    \n"
"    // Composite key (multiple keys)\n"
"    // +listType=map\n"
"    // +listMapKey=name\n"
"    // +listMapKey=protocol\n"
"    Ports []Port\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:230
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:248
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:266
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:284
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:302
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:320
msgid "By default the apiserver drops unknown fields from the request payload during the decoding step. This marker stops the API server from doing so. It affects fields recursively, but switches back to normal pruning behaviour if nested  properties or additionalProperties are specified in the schema. This can either be true or undefined. False is forbidden."
msgstr "默认情况下，apiserver 在解码步骤会丢弃请求载荷中的未知字段。此 marker 阻止 API 服务器这样做。它会递归影响字段，但若 schema 中指定了嵌套 properties 或 additionalProperties，则恢复正常裁剪行为。可为 true 或未定义。禁止为 false。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:237
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:255
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:273
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:291
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:309
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:327
msgid "NB: The kubebuilder:validation:XPreserveUnknownFields variant is deprecated in favor of the kubebuilder:pruning:PreserveUnknownFields variant.  They function identically."
msgstr "注意：kubebuilder:validation:XPreserveUnknownFields 变体已弃用，请改用 kubebuilder:pruning:PreserveUnknownFields 变体。二者功能相同。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:243
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:261
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:279
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:297
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:315
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:333
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:pruning:PreserveUnknownFields\n"
"    RawConfig map[string]interface{}\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // +kubebuilder:pruning:PreserveUnknownFields\n"
"    RawConfig map[string]interface{}\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:3
msgid "These markers describe how [webhook configuration](../webhook-overview.md) is generated. Use these to keep the description of your webhooks close to the code that implements them."
msgstr "这些标记描述了如何生成 [webhook 配置](../webhook-overview.md)。使用这些标记可以让您的 webhook 描述与实现它们的代码保持紧密关联。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:9 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:32
msgid "It specifies only the details that are intrinsic to the application serving it (e.g. the resources it can handle, or the path it serves on)."
msgstr "它仅指定服务该 webhook 的应用所固有的细节（例如它能处理的资源，或它服务的路径）。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:12 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:35
msgid "Example (Validating Webhook):"
msgstr "示例（校验 Webhook）："

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:14 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:37
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:path=/validate-mygroup-v1-myresource,mutating=false,failurePolicy=fail,sideEffects=None,groups=mygroup.example.com,resources=myresources,verbs=create;update,versions=v1,name=myresource.kb.io,admissionReviewVersions=v1\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:path=/validate-mygroup-v1-myresource,mutating=false,failurePolicy=fail,sideEffects=None,groups=mygroup.example.com,resources=myresources,verbs=create;update,versions=v1,name=myresource.kb.io,admissionReviewVersions=v1\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:16 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:39
msgid "Example (Mutating Webhook):"
msgstr "示例（变更 Webhook）："

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:18 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:41
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:path=/mutate-mygroup-v1-myresource,mutating=true,failurePolicy=fail,sideEffects=None,groups=mygroup.example.com,resources=myresources,verbs=create;update,versions=v1,name=myresource.kb.io,admissionReviewVersions=v1\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:path=/mutate-mygroup-v1-myresource,mutating=true,failurePolicy=fail,sideEffects=None,groups=mygroup.example.com,resources=myresources,verbs=create;update,versions=v1,name=myresource.kb.io,admissionReviewVersions=v1\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:22 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:68
msgid "Mutating webhooks are allowed to change the object in their response, and are called _before_ all validating webhooks.  Mutating webhooks may choose to reject an object, similarly to a validating webhook."
msgstr "Mutating webhook 允许在响应中更改对象，并在所有 validating webhook _之前_ 调用。Mutating webhook 也可以像 validating webhook 一样选择拒绝对象。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:28 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:74
msgid "Example: \"myresource.mygroup.example.com\"."
msgstr "示例：\"myresource.mygroup.example.com\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:45
msgid "versions the Webhook expects. The API server will try to use the first version in the list which it supports. If none of the versions specified are supported, the API call will fail. Common values: \"v1\" or \"v1;v1beta1\"."
msgstr "Webhook 期望的版本。API 服务器会尝试使用列表中它支持的第一个版本。若指定的版本均不受支持，API 调用将失败。常见值：\"v1\" 或 \"v1;v1beta1\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:51
msgid "It may be either \"ignore\" (to skip the webhook and continue on) or \"fail\" (to reject the object in question). Most webhooks should use \"fail\" to ensure the webhook logic is always executed."
msgstr "可以是 \"ignore\"（跳过 webhook 并继续）或 \"fail\"（拒绝相关对象）。大多数 webhook 应使用 \"fail\" 以确保始终执行 webhook 逻辑。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:57
msgid "Use \"_\" to match all groups. Multiple groups are separated by semicolons. Example: \"apps;batch\" or \"_\"."
msgstr "使用 \"_\" 匹配所有 group。多个 group 用分号分隔。示例：\"apps;batch\" 或 \"_\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:62
msgid "Allowed values are \"Exact\" (match only if it exactly matches the specified rule) or \"Equivalent\" (match a request if it modifies a resource listed in rules, even via another API group or version). Defaults to \"Equivalent\" if not specified."
msgstr "允许的值为 \"Exact\"（仅当完全匹配指定规则时匹配）或 \"Equivalent\"（若请求修改 rules 中列出的资源则匹配，即使通过另一 API group 或 version）。未指定时默认为 \"Equivalent\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:78
msgid "This allows you to set any webhook field that isn't directly exposed as a marker parameter, such as namespaceSelector, objectSelector, or matchConditions. The patch is a JSON object that follows Kubernetes strategic merge patch semantics and is applied to the webhook configuration after all other marker parameters are processed."
msgstr "这允许你设置未直接作为 marker 参数公开的任意 webhook 字段，例如 namespaceSelector、objectSelector 或 matchConditions。该补丁是遵循 Kubernetes strategic merge patch 语义的 JSON 对象，在处理完所有其他 marker 参数后应用到 webhook 配置。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:83
msgid "Use backticks to avoid escaping quotes in the JSON."
msgstr "使用反引号以避免在 JSON 中转义引号。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:85
msgid "Common use cases:"
msgstr "常见用例："

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:86
msgid "Limit webhook scope to specific namespaces using namespaceSelector"
msgstr "使用 namespaceSelector 将 Webhook 作用域限制到特定命名空间"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:87
msgid "Filter webhook invocations by object labels using objectSelector"
msgstr "使用 objectSelector 按对象标签过滤 Webhook 调用"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:88
msgid "Combine multiple customizations in a single patch"
msgstr "在单个补丁中组合多个自定义"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:90
msgid "Example (limit to labeled namespaces):"
msgstr "示例（限制到带标签的命名空间）："

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:92
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:path=/mutate-v1-pod,mutating=true,...,patch=`{\"namespaceSelector\":{\"matchLabels\":{\"webhook-enabled\":\"true\"}}}`\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:path=/mutate-v1-pod,mutating=true,...,patch=`{\"namespaceSelector\":{\"matchLabels\":{\"webhook-enabled\":\"true\"}}}`\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:94
msgid "Example (filter by object labels with matchExpressions):"
msgstr "示例（使用 matchExpressions 按对象标签过滤）："

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:96
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:path=/validate-v1-deployment,...,patch=`{\"objectSelector\":{\"matchExpressions\":[{\"key\":\"tier\",\"operator\":\"In\",\"values\":[\"frontend\",\"backend\"]}]}}`\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:path=/validate-v1-deployment,...,patch=`{\"objectSelector\":{\"matchExpressions\":[{\"key\":\"tier\",\"operator\":\"In\",\"values\":[\"frontend\",\"backend\"]}]}}`\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:98
msgid "Example (combine namespace and object selectors):"
msgstr "示例（组合命名空间与对象选择器）："

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:100
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:...,patch=`{\"namespaceSelector\":{\"matchLabels\":{\"env\":\"production\"}},\"objectSelector\":{\"matchLabels\":{\"managed-by\":\"my-operator\"}}}`\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:...,patch=`{\"namespaceSelector\":{\"matchLabels\":{\"env\":\"production\"}},\"objectSelector\":{\"matchLabels\":{\"managed-by\":\"my-operator\"}}}`\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:102
msgid "Example (override timeout):"
msgstr "示例（覆盖超时）："

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:104
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:...,patch=`{\"timeoutSeconds\":25}`\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:...,patch=`{\"timeoutSeconds\":25}`\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:106
msgid "Example (remove a field by setting it to null):"
msgstr "示例（通过设为 null 移除字段）："

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:108
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:...,patch=`{\"timeoutSeconds\":null}`\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // +kubebuilder:webhook:...,patch=`{\"timeoutSeconds\":null}`\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:110
msgid "Setting a field to null removes it. Patching a list field without a merge key, such as rules, replaces the whole list. Field names are case-sensitive and unknown fields in the patch cause an error."
msgstr "将字段设为 null 会移除它。对没有 merge key 的列表字段（如 rules）打补丁会替换整个列表。字段名区分大小写，补丁中的未知字段会导致错误。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:116
msgid "prefixed with a '/validate-' or '/mutate-' depending on the type, and followed by $GROUP-$VERSION-$KIND where all values are lower-cased and the periods in the group are substituted for hyphens. For example, a validating webhook path for type batch.tutorial.kubebuilder.io/v1,Kind=CronJob would be /validate-batch-tutorial-kubebuilder-io-v1-cronjob"
msgstr "根据类型加上 '/validate-' 或 '/mutate-' 前缀，后接 $GROUP-$VERSION-$KIND，其中所有值均为小写，group 中的句点替换为连字符。例如，类型 batch.tutorial.kubebuilder.io/v1,Kind=CronJob 的 validating webhook 路径为 /validate-batch-tutorial-kubebuilder-io-v1-cronjob"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:124
msgid "To allow mutating admission plugins to observe changes made by other plugins, built-in mutating admission plugins are re-run if a mutating webhook modifies an object, and mutating webhooks can specify a reinvocationPolicy to control whether they are reinvoked as well. May be \"Never\" or \"IfNeeded\". Defaults to \"Never\"."
msgstr "为使 mutating admission 插件能观察到其他插件所做的更改，若 mutating webhook 修改了对象，内置 mutating admission 插件会重新运行；mutating webhook 也可指定 reinvocationPolicy 以控制是否被再次调用。可为 \"Never\" 或 \"IfNeeded\"。默认为 \"Never\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:131
msgid "Use \"_\" to match all resources. Multiple resources are separated by semicolons. Example: \"deployments;pods\" or \"_\"."
msgstr "使用 \"_\" 匹配所有资源。多个资源用分号分隔。示例：\"deployments;pods\" 或 \"_\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:136
msgid "Defaults to \"webhook-service\" if not specified."
msgstr "未指定时默认为 \"webhook-service\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:140
msgid "Defaults to \"system\" if not specified."
msgstr "未指定时默认为 \"system\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:144
msgid "Defaults to 443 if not specified."
msgstr "未指定时默认为 443。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:148
msgid "This has an impact on dry runs and `kubectl diff`: if the sideEffect is \"Unknown\" (the default) or \"Some\", then the API server will not call the webhook on a dry-run request and fails instead. If the value is \"None\", then the webhook has no side effects and the API server will call it on dry-run. If the value is \"NoneOnDryRun\", then the webhook is responsible for inspecting the \"dryRun\" property of the AdmissionReview sent in the request, and avoiding side effects if that value is \"true.\" Most webhooks should use \"None\"."
msgstr "这会影响 dry run 和 `kubectl diff`：若 sideEffect 为 \"Unknown\"（默认）或 \"Some\"，则 API 服务器不会在 dry-run 请求上调用 webhook，而是失败。若值为 \"None\"，则 webhook 无副作用，API 服务器会在 dry-run 时调用它。若值为 \"NoneOnDryRun\"，则 webhook 负责检查请求中 AdmissionReview 的 \"dryRun\" 属性，并在该值为 \"true\" 时避免副作用。大多数 webhook 应使用 \"None\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:157
msgid "If the timeout expires before the webhook responds, the webhook call will be ignored or the API call will be rejected based on the failure policy. The timeout value must be between 1 and 30 seconds. The timeout for an admission webhook defaults to 10 seconds."
msgstr "若在 webhook 响应前超时到期，将根据 failure policy 忽略 webhook 调用或拒绝 API 调用。超时值必须在 1 到 30 秒之间。admission webhook 的超时默认 10 秒。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:163
msgid "the manifests, instead of using the internal service communication. Should be in format of https://address:port/path When this option is specified, the serviceConfig.Service is removed from webhook the manifest. The URL configuration should be between quotes. `url` cannot be specified when `path` is specified."
msgstr "清单中使用外部 URL，而非内部服务通信。格式应为 https://address:port/path。指定此选项时，会从 webhook 清单中移除 serviceConfig.Service。URL 配置应放在引号中。指定 `path` 时不能指定 `url`。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:171
msgid "Only modification-like verbs may be specified. May be \"create\", \"update\", \"delete\", \"connect\", or \"\\*\" (for all). Multiple verbs are separated by semicolons. Example: \"create;update\"."
msgstr "只能指定类似修改的动词。可为 \"create\"、\"update\"、\"delete\"、\"connect\" 或 \"\\*\"（表示全部）。多个动词用分号分隔。示例：\"create;update\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:177
msgid "Use \"_\" to match all versions. Multiple versions are separated by semicolons. Example: \"v1;v1beta1\" or \"_\"."
msgstr "使用 \"_\" 匹配所有版本。多个版本用分号分隔。示例：\"v1;v1beta1\" 或 \"_\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:182
msgid "itself to generate. The only supported value is v1. Defaults to v1."
msgstr "自身生成。唯一支持的值是 v1。默认为 v1。"

#: src/reference/markers/object.md:3
msgid "These markers control when `DeepCopy` and `runtime.Object` implementation methods are generated."
msgstr "这些标记控制何时生成 `DeepCopy` 和 `runtime.Object` 实现方法。"

#: src/reference/markers/applyconfiguration.md:3
msgid "These markers control when ApplyConfiguration types are generated for the kinds in a package. These types provide a type-safe way to build patches for [Server-Side Apply](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/using-api/server-side-apply/)."
msgstr "这些 markers 控制何时为包中的 kind 生成 ApplyConfiguration 类型。这些类型为构建 [Server-Side Apply](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/using-api/server-side-apply/) 补丁提供了类型安全的方式。"

#: src/reference/markers/applyconfiguration.md:7
msgid "See the [Server-Side Apply](../server-side-apply.md) reference for how the `--ssa` flag enables this generation and for examples of using the generated types."
msgstr "关于 `--ssa` 标志如何启用此生成，以及如何使用生成类型的示例，请参阅 [Server-Side Apply](../server-side-apply.md) 参考。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:3
msgid "These markers cause an [RBAC ClusterRole](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/rbac/#role-and-clusterrole) to be generated.  This allows you to describe the permissions that your controller requires alongside the code that makes use of those permissions."
msgstr "这些标记会生成一个 [RBAC ClusterRole](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/rbac/#role-and-clusterrole)。这使您能够在使用这些权限的代码旁边描述您的控制器所需的权限。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:11
msgid "RBAC markers are used to generate ClusterRole or Role manifests. Multiple markers can be combined to build comprehensive RBAC policies."
msgstr "RBAC markers 用于生成 ClusterRole 或 Role manifests。可组合多个 markers 以构建完整的 RBAC 策略。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:16
msgid ""
"    // Basic resource access\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments,verbs=get;list;watch\n"
"    \n"
"    // Core API group (use empty string)\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=&#34;&#34;,resources=pods;services,verbs=get;list;watch\n"
"    \n"
"    // Multiple API groups and resources\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps;batch,resources=deployments;jobs,verbs=get;list;watch;create;update;patch;delete\n"
"    \n"
"    // Access to resource status or scale subresources\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments/status,verbs=get;update;patch\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments/scale,verbs=get;update\n"
"    \n"
"    // Access to specific resource instances by name\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=&#34;&#34;,resources=configmaps,resourceNames=my-config,verbs=get\n"
"    \n"
"    // Non-resource URLs (for metrics, healthz, etc.)\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:urls=/metrics;/healthz,verbs=get\n"
"    \n"
"    // Namespace-scoped Role instead of ClusterRole\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=&#34;&#34;,namespace=my-namespace,resources=secrets,verbs=get;list;watch\n"
"    \n"
"    // Custom role name\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments,verbs=get;list,roleName=deployment-reader\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"    // Basic resource access\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments,verbs=get;list;watch\n"
"    \n"
"    // Core API group (use empty string)\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=&#34;&#34;,resources=pods;services,verbs=get;list;watch\n"
"    \n"
"    // Multiple API groups and resources\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps;batch,resources=deployments;jobs,verbs=get;list;watch;create;update;patch;delete\n"
"    \n"
"    // Access to resource status or scale subresources\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments/status,verbs=get;update;patch\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments/scale,verbs=get;update\n"
"    \n"
"    // Access to specific resource instances by name\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=&#34;&#34;,resources=configmaps,resourceNames=my-config,verbs=get\n"
"    \n"
"    // Non-resource URLs (for metrics, healthz, etc.)\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:urls=/metrics;/healthz,verbs=get\n"
"    \n"
"    // Namespace-scoped Role instead of ClusterRole\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=&#34;&#34;,namespace=my-namespace,resources=secrets,verbs=get;list;watch\n"
"    \n"
"    // Custom role name\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments,verbs=get;list,roleName=deployment-reader\n"
"    "

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:43
msgid "Use empty string (\"\") for the core API group. Multiple groups can be specified separated by semicolons. Example: \"apps;batch\" or \"\" (for core group)."
msgstr "核心 API group 使用空字符串（\"\"）。可用分号分隔指定多个 group。示例：\"apps;batch\" 或 \"\"（表示核心 group）。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:49
msgid "If not set, the Rule belongs to the generated ClusterRole. If set, the Rule belongs to a Role, whose namespace is specified by this field. Example: \"my-namespace\"."
msgstr "若未设置，Rule 属于生成的 ClusterRole。若设置，Rule 属于 Role，其命名空间由此字段指定。示例：\"my-namespace\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:55
msgid "Create requests cannot be restricted by resourcename, as the object's name is not known at authorization time. Multiple names can be specified separated by semicolons. Example: \"my-config;my-secret\"."
msgstr "Create 请求不能按 resourcename 限制，因为授权时对象名称尚未知。可用分号分隔指定多个名称。示例：\"my-config;my-secret\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:62
msgid "Multiple resources can be specified separated by semicolons. Subresources can be specified with a slash (e.g., \"deployments/status\"). Example: \"deployments;pods\" or \"deployments/status\"."
msgstr "可用分号分隔指定多个资源。子资源可用斜杠指定（例如 \"deployments/status\"）。示例：\"deployments;pods\" 或 \"deployments/status\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:68
msgid "If not set, uses the default roleName from the generator. Useful for avoiding name conflicts when the same roleName is used across multiple namespaces."
msgstr "若未设置，使用生成器的默认 roleName。在多个命名空间使用相同 roleName 时，有助于避免名称冲突。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:71
msgid "Example: When using namespace-scoped RBAC markers with kustomize's global namespace transformation, multiple Roles might end up in the same namespace with identical names, causing an \"ID conflict\" error. Use roleName to ensure each Role has a unique name:"
msgstr "示例：当将命名空间作用域的 RBAC markers 与 kustomize 的全局命名空间转换一起使用时，多个 Role 可能最终出现在同一命名空间且名称相同，导致 \"ID conflict\" 错误。使用 roleName 确保每个 Role 有唯一名称："

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:75
msgid "// +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,namespace=infrastructure,roleName=infra-manager,resources=deployments,verbs=get;list // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=\"\",namespace=users,roleName=user-secrets,resources=secrets,verbs=get"
msgstr "// +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,namespace=infrastructure,roleName=infra-manager,resources=deployments,verbs=get;list // +kubebuilder:rbac:groups=\"\",namespace=users,roleName=user-secrets,resources=secrets,verbs=get"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:78
msgid "This generates Roles named \"infra-manager\" and \"user-secrets\" instead of both being \"manager-role\"."
msgstr "这将生成名为 \"infra-manager\" 和 \"user-secrets\" 的 Role，而不是都叫 \"manager-role\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:82
msgid "Non-resource URLs are paths that don't represent resources, like \"/metrics\" or \"/healthz\". Multiple URLs can be specified separated by semicolons. Example: \"/metrics;/healthz\"."
msgstr "非资源 URL 是不表示资源的路径，如 \"/metrics\" 或 \"/healthz\"。可用分号分隔指定多个 URL。示例：\"/metrics;/healthz\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:88
msgid "Common verbs: \"get\", \"list\", \"watch\", \"create\", \"update\", \"patch\", \"delete\". Use \"\\*\" for all verbs. Multiple verbs must be specified separated by semicolons. Example: \"get;list;watch\"."
msgstr "常见动词：\"get\"、\"list\"、\"watch\"、\"create\"、\"update\"、\"patch\"、\"delete\"。使用 \"\\*\" 表示全部动词。多个动词必须用分号分隔。示例：\"get;list;watch\"。"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:3
msgid "The `+kubebuilder:scaffold` marker is a key part of the Kubebuilder scaffolding system. It marks locations in generated files where Kubebuilder injects additional code as you scaffold new resources (such as controllers, webhooks, or APIs). This enables Kubebuilder to seamlessly integrate newly generated components into the project without affecting user-defined code."
msgstr "`+kubebuilder:scaffold` 标记是 Kubebuilder 脚手架系统的一个关键部分。它标记了生成文件中将注入额外代码的位置，当新的资源（如控制器、webhook 或 API）被脚手架生成时。这使得 Kubebuilder 能够无缝地将新生成的组件集成到项目中，而不影响用户定义的代码。"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:11
msgid "The Kubebuilder CLI specifically looks for these markers in expected files during code generation. If the marker is moved or removed, the CLI will not be able to inject the necessary code, and the scaffolding process may fail or behave unexpectedly."
msgstr "Kubebuilder CLI 在代码生成期间会特别查找预期文件中的这些标记。如果标记被移动或移除，CLI 将无法注入必要的代码，搭建过程可能会失败或表现得不符合预期。"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:20
msgid "When you scaffold a new resource using the Kubebuilder CLI (e.g., `kubebuilder create api`), the CLI identifies `+kubebuilder:scaffold` markers in key locations and uses them as placeholders to insert the required imports and registration code."
msgstr "当您使用 Kubebuilder CLI （例如，`kubebuilder create api`）搭建新的资源时，CLI 会在关键位置识别 `+kubebuilder:scaffold` 标记，并将其作为占位符，用于插入所需的导入和注册代码。"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:24
msgid "Example usage in `main.go`"
msgstr "`main.go` 中的示例用法"

