msgstr "以下条目将被添加到项目文件中："

#: src/plugins/extending/extending_cli_features_and_plugins.md:441
msgid "By inspecting the PROJECT file, it becomes possible to understand how the plugin was used and what inputs were provided. This not only allows re-execution of the command based on the tracked data but also enables creating features or plugins that can rely on this information."
msgstr "通过检查 PROJECT 文件，可以了解插件是如何使用的以及提供了哪些输入。这不仅可以基于跟踪的数据重新执行命令，还能够创建可以依赖这些信息的功能或插件。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:1
msgid "Creating external plugins for Kubebuilder"
msgstr "为 Kubebuilder 创建外部插件"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:5
msgid "Kubebuilder's functionality can be extended through external plugins. These plugins are executables (written in any language) that follow an execution pattern recognized by Kubebuilder. Kubebuilder interacts with these plugins via `stdin` and `stdout`, enabling seamless communication."
msgstr "Kubebuilder 的功能可以通过外部插件进行扩展。这些插件是可执行文件（可以用任何语言编写），遵循 Kubebuilder 认可的执行模式。Kubebuilder 通过 `stdin` 和 `stdout` 与这些插件进行交互，实现无缝通信。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:10
msgid "Why use external plugins?"
msgstr "为什么使用外部插件？"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:12
msgid "External plugins enable third-party solution maintainers to integrate their tools with Kubebuilder. Much like Kubebuilder's own plugins, these can be opt-in, offering users flexibility in tool selection. By developing plugins in their repositories, maintainers ensure updates are aligned with their CI pipelines and can manage any changes within their domain of responsibility."
msgstr "外部插件使第三方解决方案维护者能够将其工具与 Kubebuilder 集成。与 Kubebuilder 自身的插件类似，这些插件可以选择性使用，为用户提供工具选择的灵活性。通过在自己的代码库中开发插件，维护者确保更新与其 CI 流水线保持一致，并能够管理其责任范围内的任何变更。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:18
msgid "If you are interested in this type of integration, collaborating with the maintainers of the third-party solution is recommended. Kubebuilder's maintainers are always willing to provide support in extending its capabilities."
msgstr "如果您对这种类型的集成感兴趣，建议与第三方解决方案的维护者进行合作。Kubebuilder 的维护者始终乐意提供支持，以扩展其功能。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:22
msgid "How to Write an External Plugin"
msgstr "如何编写外部插件"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:24
msgid "Communication between Kubebuilder and an external plugin occurs via standard I/O. Any language can be used to create the plugin, as long as it follows the [PluginRequest](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/book-v4/pkg/plugin/external/types.go) and [PluginResponse](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/book-v4/pkg/plugin/external/types.go) structures."
msgstr "Kubebuilder 与外部插件之间的通信通过标准输入/输出进行。可以使用任何语言创建插件，只要它遵循 [PluginRequest](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/book-v4/pkg/plugin/external/types.go) 和 [PluginResponse](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/book-v4/pkg/plugin/external/types.go) 结构。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:29
msgid "`PluginRequest` contains the data collected from the CLI and any previously executed plugins. Kubebuilder sends this data as a JSON object to the external plugin via `stdin`."
msgstr "`PluginRequest`包含从CLI收集的数据以及之前执行的插件。Kubebuilder通过`stdin`将这些数据作为JSON对象发送给外部插件。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:31
msgid "**Fields:**"
msgstr "**Fields:**"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:32
msgid "`apiVersion`: Version of the PluginRequest schema."
msgstr "`apiVersion`：PluginRequest schema 的版本。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:33
msgid "`args`: Command-line arguments passed to the plugin."
msgstr "`args`：传递给插件的命令行参数。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:34
msgid "`command`: The subcommand being executed (e.g., `init`, `create api`, `create webhook`, `edit`)."
msgstr "`command`：正在执行的子命令（例如 `init`、`create api`、`create webhook`、`edit`）。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:35
msgid "`universe`: Map of file paths to contents, updated across the plugin chain."
msgstr "`universe`：文件路径到内容的映射，在插件链中更新。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:36
msgid "`pluginChain` (optional): Array of plugin keys in the order they were executed. External plugins can inspect this to tailor behavior based on other plugins that ran (for example, `go.kubebuilder.io/v4` or `kustomize.common.kubebuilder.io/v2`)."
msgstr "`pluginChain`（可选）：按执行顺序列出的插件键数组。外部插件可检查此项，以便根据已运行的其他插件（例如 `go.kubebuilder.io/v4` 或 `kustomize.common.kubebuilder.io/v2`）调整行为。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:37
msgid "`config` (optional): Serialized PROJECT file configuration for the current project. Use it to inspect metadata, existing resources, or plugin-specific settings. Kubebuilder omits this field before the PROJECT file exists—typically during the first `init`—so plugins should check for its presence."
msgstr "`config`（可选）：当前项目的序列化 PROJECT 文件配置。用于检查元数据、现有资源或插件特定设置。在 PROJECT 文件存在之前——通常是第一次 `init`——Kubebuilder 会省略此字段，因此插件应检查其是否存在。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:40
msgid "**Note:** Whenever Kubebuilder has a PROJECT file available (for example during `create api`, `create webhook`, `edit`, or a subsequent `init` run), `PluginRequest` includes the `config` field. During the very first `init` run the field is omitted because the PROJECT file does not exist yet."
msgstr "**注意：** 只要 Kubebuilder 可访问 PROJECT 文件（例如在 `create api`、`create webhook`、`edit` 或后续 `init` 运行期间），`PluginRequest` 就会包含 `config` 字段。在非常第一次 `init` 运行时该字段会被省略，因为 PROJECT 文件尚不存在。"

#: src/plugins/extending/external-plugins.md:42
msgid "**Example `PluginRequest` (triggered by `kubebuilder init --plugins go/v4,sampleexternalplugin/v1 --domain my.domain`):**"
msgstr "**示例 `PluginRequest`（通过 `kubebuilder init --plugins sampleexternalplugin/v1 --domain my.domain` 触发）：**"

